*[[File:Note About Jane No Mercy Message.png|thumb|250px|[[Kthara]] sends a message]]At the [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]] in [[Portland]], Dr. [[Louise Hastings]] types up a patient's psychiatric evaluation. Her desk candle goes out and the door opens by itself, then her keyboard starts typing on its own, writing "NO MERCY" repeatedly, and glass shatters. She finds a guard murdered and has the center locked down, but nurse [[Keith Spivey]] has escaped with patients [[Hock]] and [[Liddle]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*In [[Salem (Oregon)|Salem]], [[Gabriella Rosetti]] assures [[Mr. Cavallo]] that her associate, [[Daimon Helstrom]], is coming. Helstrom arrives and Mr. Cavallo takes him and Rosetti into his home to help with his son, [[Archer Cavallo|Archer]]'s possible possession. Helstrom rejects the offer of a Bible and visits the restroom before ascending the stairs to Archer's room.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*[[File:Daimon Sets Fire Circle.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] sets fire in front of [[Archer Cavallo]]]] Helstrom finds Archer Cavallo exclaiming threats, and tells the boy that he has water from the [[Vatican City|Vatican]], sprinkling him with it. Cavallo claims to be cured and not remember anything, but Helstrom reveals it was just water from the restroom, having exposed Cavallo for having lied and put on an act. Cavallo is angry and goes to punch Helstrom, but Helstrom uses his abilities to immobilize the boy and briefly create a ring of fire, scaring him, before leaving.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*As Helstrom leaves the house with Rosetti, he tells the Cavallos that their son was lying and that they have been incompetent parents. Rosetti tells him he is too insensitive, but he explains he cannot help that type of family and leaves to return to Portland.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*In [[San Francisco]], [[Ana Helstrom]] holds an auction with her friend and colleague [[Chris Yen]], where they spot their target, [[Edward Tate]], in attendance to bid on a sword of {{WPS|Napoleon}}'s. Helstrom reminds Yen to kill the security feeds for their plan.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*'''[[Assassination of Edward Tate]]''': Ana Helstrom talks to Tate after the auction, pretending to flirt with him. She then reveals she procured Napoleon's sword just to lure him there, revealing she knows he has killed seven women. She uses her powers to make him choke, before shoving him off the balcony to his death.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*[[File:KSpiveyBleedingMouthDeathScene.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Keith Spivey]] is killed]]'''[[Liberation of Basar]]''': In [[Colma]], Keith Spivey, with the help of Hock and Liddle, breaks into hidden catacombs under a temple. He finds a sarcophagus bearing the symbol he has a photograph of on his phone, and tries to open it. However, Hock then presses Spivey's head to the sarcophagus, drawing blood. Spokes on the sarcophagus unwrap before clawing Spivey in, as Liddle announces that this is why he and Hock were chosen.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Ana Helstrom uses a dating app to have a one-night stand with a woman whose name begins with B to help relieve her stress.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}

====14th====
*[[Cameron Tate]] is named CEO and COO of [[Edward Tate]]'s company, stabilizing the company's sudden stock decline.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*At [[Gateway University]], Daimon Helstrom delivers a lecture on pain, fear, and {{WPS|Lawrence Kohlberg}}'s stages of moral development. He notices Louise Hastings at the door, coming to visit.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*[[File:Daimon and Hastings Catch Up.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] talks to [[Louise Hastings]]]] After his lecture, Helstrom walks with Hastings, complaining that Rosetti is not good enough at determining real possessions and saying that he wished Hastings were still on the job. Hastings explains that she has come to tell him that his [[Victoria Helstrom|mother]]'s [[Kthara|demon]] helped a nurse and two patients escape Saint Teresa's the night before and that a guard was killed. She requests his help, since he is the only one who can talk to the demon, and Helstrom offers to pay the guard's funeral costs.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*The [[San Francisco Police Department]] find a suicide note on Edward Tate's body, leaving them to rule his death a suicide.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Ana Helstrom arrives at work, where Yen tells her that he has successfully kept the auction out of the news, but complains she is being reckless. She finds she has a missed call from [[Caretaker]], and Yen explains he also visited, having mentioned a crib in Colma.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*At Saint Teresa's, Daimon Helstrom and Hastings are joined by Gabriella Rosetti. Hastings shows them the security footage of Spivey's escape. Helstrom decides to visit his "mother", and Rosetti insists on joining so she can report to the Vatican, but he refuses her company.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Helstrom enters his "mother's" cell, where he notices the symbol she has drawn on the wall and tries to talk to her. He attempts to jolt his mother's memory with a story of her kindness from his childhood. She appears to respond, but it is the demon taunting him. The demon claims Helstrom's memories are tainted by sentiment, and that his mother had tried to abort him by drinking. He inquires about the events of the night before and she eventually says she sent [[Keith Spivey]] and the patients to see "an old friend", before declaring the conversation to be finished.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Information about "Tate's suicide note" are leaked, saying that the note contains a confession to several murders. The lead police detective on the murders refuses to comment beyond saying that the murders could have been related.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Ana Sees Keeper's Skull.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] finds [[Keeper's Skull]]]] [[Ana Helstrom]] visits [[Caretaker]] in the [[Colma]] cemetery on his request, where he explains he did not know about the hidden cave until the night before. She asks where he has been, and he explains he has been in [[Texas]], tracking [[Ghost Rider|something]],<ref>[https://deadline.com/2019/08/marvel-jeph-loeb-interview-disney-legion-netflix-runaways-ghost-rider-howard-the-duck-hulu-1202666578/ Marvel TV Boss Jeph Loeb On Secret ABC Series, Disney+, ‘Legion’ End, More Crossovers, ‘Ghost Rider’ & Hulu Plans]</ref><ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/live-action-ghost-rider-and-helstrom-tv-series-heading-to-hulu-in-2020?linkId=66795246 Live-Action Ghost Rider and Helstrom TV Series Heading to Hulu in 2020]</ref> then takes her to the catacombs.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*As Helstrom and Caretaker investigate, they see the remains of the people who came the night before. Caretaker shows her the sarcophagus, which is broken open with a skeleton inside with only one eye - ancient and demonic. Caretaker identifies it as a [[Keeper Demons|Keeper]], and they wonder whether it could have been keeping [[Marduk Kurios|Helstrom's father]] at bay. She nonetheless refuses to reach out to her brother. Caretaker warns Helstrom not to touch anything, but she decides to take the [[Keeper's Skull]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*<!--20:07 West coast, so 23:07 East coast-->[[File:Gabby Argues About Seeing Kthara.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] talks about [[Kthara]]]] At the [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]], [[Daimon Helstrom]] tells [[Gabriella Rosetti]] and [[Louise Hastings]] that he knows the symbol in [[Victoria Helstrom|Victoria]]'s room was demonic in nature, and tells them about the mention of an "old friend". Rosetti wants to go in alone to verify her behavior is real, Helstrom snaps about her poor judgement with cases like [[Archer Cavallo]]. She says she has a report to write to the archbishop, and tells Helstrom she does not care for his disrespect. After she leaves, Helstrom admits to Hastings that he knows he is being rude, and Hastings reminds him they need Rosetti's help. Helstrom admits his frustration at being unable to help his mother and ponders asking for his sister's help, though considers reaching out likely pointless.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Rosetti contacts the bishop of the archdiocese with an update about Saint Teresa's and Helstrom.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}

====15th====
*<!--22:57 West coast, so 01:57 East coast-->At 22:57 on the 14th local time, Daimon Helstrom reaches out to Ana by text asking to talk. She reads the message, but puts her phone aside and decides to get back to work.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*[[File:Daimon Scar Tattoo.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] tattoos over the scar]] During the night, Daimon Helstrom goes to a tattoo parlor to get a tattoo over his chest scar, but the artist struggles with the scar, commenting on how the ink just disappears on it. He asks her to just keep trying.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Ana Helstrom decides to cut her finger and smear blood on the Keeper's skull. She holds her hand to it to see how it will respond, then is scared when she sees an eyeball jump up from its empty socket. She notices her blood gravitating to the demonic symbol on the forehead, the same one from the catacomb.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*In the morning, Caretaker digs a grave to bury the remains found in the catacomb. He discovers a torn shred of clothing reading "ST. TERESA DFMH".{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Caretaker calls Ana Helstrom and tells her of his discovery, worried that her mother may be involved in the men's deaths.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Daimon Helstrom leaves a message on Gabriella Rosetti's phone, apologizing for potentially offending her the day before. He sits in  his car, parked outside the [[Cavallo Residence]], and watches as [[Mr. Cavallo]] takes [[Archer Cavallo|Archer]] out with him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Louise Hastings asks Rosetti to forgive Daimon Helstrom. Rosetti explains that the [[Vatican City|Vatican]] is concerned about Daimon performing exorcisms as well as having abilities potentially inherited from evil. Hastings tries to dismiss this concern, but Rosetti insists on seeing Victoria Helstrom. Hastings, however, gives her her pass, telling Rosetti to look at what is on her desk first.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Rosetti visits Hastings' office, where she finds a binder. Opening it, Rosetti sees Daimon Helstrom's children's home admissions placement form.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*[[File:Daimon Writes Consumption.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] draws]] While his class works silently, Daimon Helstrom draws the symbol from his mother's cell repeatedly.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Rosetti looks through the form, and onto Ana Helstrom's, followed by a ''[[The Oregon Examiner]]'' article about [[Kidnapping of Ana Helstrom|Ana's kidnapping]]. Meanwhile, "Victoria" lies in her cell, still possessed. At her [[Ana Helstrom's Auction House|auction house]], Ana walks carrying the Keeper Skull. At [[Gateway University]], Daimon continues to draw.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Rosetti finds more articles, from ''[[The Dallas Record]]'' and other papers, detailing murders linked to the [[Marduk Kurios|Helstrom father]]. She then finds a journal, which she opens. Meanwhile, "Victoria Helstrom" smiles emptily in her cell, Ana places the skull on a shelf in her auction house, and Daimon finds himself scrawling non-stop.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Rosetti discovers that the journal is Victoria Helstrom's from the days when her demon was taking her over, including Victoria's written exclamations at her demon in her anger and desperation. Meanwhile, Ana looks back at the shelf contemplatively, and Daimon continues to draw even after his class has left, when his page suddenly briefly combusts.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Hastings gets back to her office and explains to Rosetti that Victoria Helstrom was cursed, and that Ana is in [[San Francisco]] and does not get along with Daimon. She says the Helstroms have to live with the evil done to their family.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*<!--At least a few hours before 23:30 West coast scene, for Ana's travel-->[[File:Ana's Box Contents 2.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]]'s box]] Ana Helstrom sits down with a small chest from her youth, ruminating on her kidnapping. She tentatively opens the chest, which contains trinkets her father gave her during her time kidnapped by him, but she cannot face it for long, closing it again and pushing it away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}

====16th====
*<!--23:20ish West coast, so 02:20ish East coast-->Rosetti asks Hastings why Daimon Helstrom cannot help his mother. Hastings explains they do not know, but that they are losing Victoria to her demon due to the strain on her body. Hastings starts coughing and finds she coughs up blood, so leaves the room, merely telling Rosetti she needs a moment. Rosetti takes the opportunity to grab Hastings' ID, left on the desk, and go to visit Victoria's cell.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*<!--23:30 West coast, so 02:30 East coast-->At 23:30 on the 15th local time, Rosetti goes to the cell and lets herself in. She is attacked by "Victoria Helstrom", though tries to question her nonetheless.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Hastings checks the surveillance footage and sees where Rosetti has gone. She rushes to get her out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*[[File:Gabby Cross.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] attempts to protect herself]] "Victoria Helstrom" taunts Rosetti and uses her abilities to telekinetically slam her against the wall. Rosetti punches her, so "Victoria" then slams her into the ceiling and chokes her. Daimon and Hastings run in and Rosetti falls, but Daimon uses his ability to stop her hitting the ground hard. Hastings rushes to Rosetti's aid and Daimon comes face-to-face with "his mother". "Victoria" grabs him by the neck, but he starts trying - but struggling - to exorcise her. He demands she let Victoria go, but the demon refuses. They send each other flying back, and Victoria emerges for a moment, telling the trio to run. They get out and close the door.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*In the early hours, Hastings pours [[O'Harren's Scotch Whisky]]. She and Helstrom explain to Rosetti that demons feed on suffering. Hastings asks Helstrom how he knew to come, but he explains he had in fact come to show her his burned paper - that it had burned because the symbol drawn was an ideogram, which he translates as "consumption". Rosetti expresses how unsettled she is, but Helstrom reminds her she decided herself to go looking.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*Daimon Helstrom leaves Saint Teresa's, only to find his sister waiting for him outside, having come after all. Ana says she is hoping to hear that their mother is dead.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS101}}
*[[File:BasarRevealingHisHalfFace.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Basar]] attacks]] [[Alex Tilden]] leaves a [[Roxxon Gas Station]] after a brief stop, only to find a man has broken into his truck. The man, the bloodied and possessed [[Keith Spivey]], suddenly turns and attacks him.{{Ref|HS101}} "Spivey" marks Tilden for possession by the demon [[Magoth]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*The Helstrom siblings visit [[The Blue Heron Restaurant]] to talk. Daimon asks why she has come now, and Ana claims she just figured things must be serious. He asks for her help trying to pull the demon out of their mother and to reconnect as siblings, but Ana is uninterested. He demands to know why she really came, and she says that if their mother is going to die, she wants permission to see her alone and get things off her chest. Daimon eventually accepts. He tells her about his ethics lecturing job and invites her to stay with him, but she leaves for her suite at [[The Nines Hotel]]{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Kevin Wants to Help.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Kevin (Driver)|Kevin]] tries to help]] In the morning, Alex Tilden lies dying on the road. A man, [[Kevin (Driver)|Kevin]], stops to help him, and Tilden asks for a hospital.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*<!--Morning-->[[Chris Yen]] has to give a client appraisal without [[Ana Helstrom]]. When he is asked if a battle axe they own belonged to {{WPS|Attila}}, he does not know, without her around to help.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*<!--Morning-->[[Daimon Helstrom]] talks to [[Louise Hastings]] about Ana potentially visiting [[Victoria Helstrom|Victoria]]. Hastings tells him it is a bad idea.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*<!--Afternoon-->[[File:Yen with Antiques.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] calls [[Ana Helstrom]]]] Chris Yen calls Ana Helstrom, letting her know that their fake suicide note for [[Edward Tate]] has worked and that she has missed a client appraisal. She tells him she is dealing with something personal and will not be back for a day or two, then hangs up as she arrives at the [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Hastings meets with Ana Helstrom, telling her that she disapproves of her visiting her mother. She insists on at least accompanying Helstrom. Helstrom threatens her, but Hastings is unfazed.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*As Kevin drives Tilden to hospital, Tilden starts to moan and writhe in the backseat. "Tilden", in fact possessed by Magoth, suddenly attacks Kevin, causing the car to swerve as a truck comes at them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*"Tilden" is the only survivor of the accident, and is dying. Father [[Sean Okamoto]] is called to give last rites, but upon arrival, "Tilden" bites him. The demon inside Tilden telekinetically detaches a car side mirror and flings it at Okamoto.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Ana and Hastings Thrown to Wall.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] and [[Louise Hastings]] are thrown]] Ana Helstrom and Hastings enter Victoria's cell and Ana inspects her expressionless mother. Hastings explains how Daimon uses happy childhood memories to briefly coax Victoria out, suggesting this to Ana, but instead Ana slaps her mother. The demon reacts by telekinetically throwing the women back and into the wall.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[Gabriella Rosetti]] arrives at Saint Teresa's, where she receives a call about a strange phenomenon from Father Okamoto. She sees Daimon Helstrom arriving and calls to him, but he ignores her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Ana and Damion Helstrom.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom|Daimon]] and [[Ana Helstrom]] argue]] Daimon Helstrom confronts his sister about what she did. He accuses her of no empathy and goes to say that she reminds him of their [[Marduk Kurios|father]], but stops. However, she works out what he was saying and an argument begins. As they lose control of their abilities, items start shaking, and "Victoria" senses their argument in her cell. Hastings intervenes and reminds them she is in charge at the facility, and Rosetti tells Daimon about the situation they are needed for. Ana is introduced to Rosetti and tries to flirt with her. Rosetti ignores this and explains that there is a possessed man dying and in need of help, and he reluctantly agrees to go.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*On the drive to the dying man, Daimon Helstrom explains to Rosetti that Ana did not have a career like Hastings growing up. When Rosetti asks about the Helstroms' abilities, he explains they come from their father, who was far worse than the demon inhabiting Victoria.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*At the auction house, Chris Yen places the unsold axe on a shelf. Behind him, the cloth falls from the [[Keeper's Skull]], and he turns and sees it. Fascinated, he walks to it and hears voices in his head. He reaches to touch it, but is interrupted by [[Caretaker]] and replaces the cloth. Caretaker asks where Ana Helstrom is, and he eventually explains what she said about dealing with personal matters. Caretaker surmises she went to [[Portland]], to Yen's frustration. He tells Yen the axe is fake and asks whether Helstrom took "the skull", but Yen claims not to know what he is referring to.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Continuing to drive, Daimon Helstrom tells Rosetti that Bible quotes will not protect her from a demon and is dismissive in her belief in the power of faith, before apologizing for being too rude. Rosetti tells him she worked with the {{WPS|Talitha Kum}} to combat child trafficking, pointing out that she is not naive, having already seen the worst of humanity.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Esther Meets Taker.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Esther Smith]] meets with [[Caretaker]]]] In [[San Francisco]], Caretaker meets with [[Esther Smith]]. He tells her a demon protected by a [[Keeper Demons|Keeper]] has escaped and that Ana Helstrom is in Portland. When she worries about the Helstrom siblings being together, he says he is going after her immediately. She notes that he cannot protect Ana forever, and that if she steps out of line, she has to be put down.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*A CEO dies, leaving his partner the sole person in charge of the company.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HSNewspaper1}}
*[[Gabriella Rosetti]] and [[Daimon Helstrom]] arrive and greet Father Okamoto, who explains his encounter with "[[Alex Tilden]]", and that Tilden will die the moment he is freed. Helstrom approaches, as Okamoto explains to Rosetti that Tilden's family are coming and that Helstrom needs to free Tilden's soul before he dies.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Yen Looks at Skull.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] and [[Keeper's Skull]]]] [[Chris Yen]] sits with the [[Keeper's Skull]], captivated by it. Compelled, he opens the jaw and sinks the skull's fangs into his arm, causing heavy bleeding.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[Ana Helstrom]] listens to a voicemail left by Yen, frustrated at her for not telling him where she was going. She sees [[Louise Hastings]] and insists on talking to "[[Victoria Helstrom|Victoria]]" again. Hastings refuses. Ana explains that she is aware of Hastings' decision to split them up as children and threatens to tell Daimon, but Hastings says she does not know what she is talking about and that "Victoria" will overwhelm her if she is not careful.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Daimon Helstrom and Rosetti approach "Tilden". Helstrom notes that it is a bad idea for Tilden's family to come, as they will only see Tilden possessed and once he is exorcised, he will die. He shows Rosetti the "mark" on Tilden's body, explaining that the oldest and most powerful demons mark hosts to allow other demons to possess them, then absorb the victims' energy at the point of death. He explains they should try to find whoever marked him. "Tilden" starts mocking them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Hastings reluctantly accompanies Ana Helstrom in another cell visit, and Ana tries to provoke her mother's demon. She whispers that it might be better if it were just the two of them, then "Victoria" uses her power to make Hastings cough.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Gabby Listens to Alex.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] looks at [[Alex Tilden]]]] At the crash site, "Tilden" uses his power to telekinetically hurl a truck door at Rosetti, but Helstrom telekinetically deflects it. "Tilden" reveals all demons know Helstrom, calling him "traitor". He reveals his name is [[Magoth]], and notes the arrival of Tilden's family, taunting that Tilden had been cheating on his wife. He adds that Helstrom should thank his sister for sending them "so many promising new recruits".{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*At the [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]], Ana Helstrom decides to try discussing a shared childhood memory to prompt her mother. She recites how [[Marduk Kurios|Father]] bought her a green pin when she was 8, but Victoria had slapped it out of her hand - and how she blames Victoria for staying with Father. Hastings' coughing worsens and she is forced to step out, then Victoria's demon starts to respond. Ana says she is here for her, not her actual mother.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Gabriella Rosetti starts praying for Alex Tilden's soul. Helstrom grabs Magoth's arm and he writhes, telekinetically moving a flare to light the spilled gasoline.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*'''[[Assassination of Cameron Tate]]''':
**[[File:Yen Asks Keeper Skull its Thoughts.png|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] is influenced by the skull]] [[Cameron Tate]] visits [[Ana Helstrom's Auction House]], insisting to Yen that his [[Edward Tate|brother]] did not commit suicide. Yen asserts his belief that Tate helped his brother in his killings. He then listens to the sounds in his head of the Keeper's Skull, walks off to get the axe from the shelf, and returns.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
**Yen hits Tate with the axe, causing him to fall. Tate tries to recover, but Yen uses the axe to pull him down by the neck, causing him to fall to the ground. Yen stabs Tate in the back. He leaves the auction house with the skull, tripping over Tate's body and leaving it behind. He closes the door to the vault, leaving behind a bit of blood and a knocked over file, and does not activate the alarm.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Victoria Helstrom's demon tries to play with Ana's feelings, but Ana is defiant and demands to know what the demon set loose on the world, threatening to "make her" talk if need be. Ana grabs hold of her mother to torture her, but finds herself unable to do anything. "Victoria" stands, drains her of energy, and lets her drop to the floor.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Daimon Helstrom faces Magoth's fire and uses his mind to part it. Meanwhile, Rosetti continues to pray for Tilden. Tilden is momentarily freed and requests she tell his family he loves them and is sorry. Magoth takes over again and warns of the one who marked him, who is coming.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Meanwhile, elsewhere, [[Basar]] consumes his latest victim.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*[[File:Alex Tilden Exorcism.png|thumb|250px|[[Alex Tilden]] is exorcised]]'''[[Exorcism of Alex Tilden]]''': Daimon Helstrom grabs [[Alex Tilden]]'s body and uses his power to exorcise Magoth. He himself is drained by the process. Once the demon is gone, the fire dissipates, and Tilden dies. Rosetti prays for the deceased man.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*In her cell, "Victoria Helstrom" strokes the unconscious Ana's hair.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Rosetti talks to Tilden's family, then gets in the car with Helstrom, saying she only told them what they needed to hear. Helstrom notes that not everybody gets closure.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}
*Ana Helstrom wakes and demands to know what was in the crypt. "Victoria" claims she sent the patients to kill what was there, not set it free, and implies the demon set loose was Ana's father, to Ana's dismay. Ana walks out in shock and fear.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS102}}

====17th====
*'''[[Massacre of Phi Gamma Epsilon]]''':
**In the early hours,{{Ref|HSNewspaper1}} [[Basar]] goes to the [[Phi Gamma Epsilon House]] at [[Gateway University]] and slaughters all of the members of the [[Phi Gamma Epsilon|fraternity]] that live there. A member, [[Chad (Frat Boy)|Chad]], runs away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
**Chad tries to hide in several rooms, finding that all of them are locked, as Basar chases him. He comes to a locked door at the end of the hallway and pleads with Basar, saying that his parents have money and offering Basar whatever he wants. Basar kills Chad anyway.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
**[[File:Basar'sBloodyHand.png|thumb|250px|[[Basar]]'s bloody hand]] Basar sits on a throne in the frat house, where [[Magoth]], now possessing the student [[Bryce (Student)|Bryce]], tells Basar that [[Daimon Helstrom]] was warned that they were coming. Basar tells Magoth that there is more to be done, asking Magoth to bring "[[Aubree Richards|the woman]]" to him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
**Basar and Magoth burn down the house, making it appear to be the cause of death for the fraternity's members. The authorities arrive and declare the situation to have been an electrical fire.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Firefighters respond to calls about the house burning down, but find the building unsalvageable as it collapses in front of them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HSNewspaper1}}
*The President of the University declares the following day to be a day of remembrance and mourning, cancelling classes and scheduling a memorial on the school's football field.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HSNewspaper1}}
*The [[United Nations]] concludes their week-long conference, which they believe will result in breakthroughs in anti-terrorism, migration movement, and economic security. The speaker announcing the conclusion stresses the importance of cooperation and following the [[Sokovia Accords]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HSNewspaper1}}
