====18th====
{{DubiousSection}}
*''[[The Oregon Examiner]]'' weekend edition front page reports on a fire at the Phi Gamma Epsilon house. Other articles include the increase in church attendance and the United Nations vowing a new era in global security following their cooperation on the [[Sokovia Accords]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HSNewspaper1}}{{Ref|HS103}}

====19th====
*[[Daimon Helstrom]] visits [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]] and discovers that [[Victoria Helstrom|Victoria]] is more lucid than she has been in years. Victoria asks about [[Ana Helstrom|Ana]] and rambles about memories from when her children were younger.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:DaimonCallsAna.png|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom|Daimon]] calls [[Ana Helstrom]]]] Ana Helstrom dreams that [[Ana Helstrom/Adult Ana Helstrom Buried|she]] is brushing her teeth when she starts choking and coughing up dirt, then collapses. She wakes up to her cell phone vibrating with a call from Daimon. She answers, and Daimon tells her about their mother's lucidity. Ana attempts to dismiss Daimon, but he explains that he needs her to help their mother. Ana says she does not think she could say anything else to her, but Daimon insists they could save Victoria. Ana reluctantly agrees to help.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Ana Helstrom goes to the lobby of [[The Nines Hotel]] and finds [[Caretaker]]. She approaches him and tells him that the [[Kthara|demon]] inside her mother confirmed that her [[Marduk Kurios|father]] is back, saying that she plans to kill him. Caretaker says that it would be too dangerous, but Ana refuses to listen or accept help. She tells Caretaker that Daimon does not know, so Caretaker advises her not to let pride get in her way. Helstrom says that she is not motivated by pride, but rather by rage.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Daimon and Ana Helstrom prepare to enter Victoria's room, and Daimon suggests that Ana follow his lead. When they enter, Victoria cries with joy upon seeing Ana, happy that her children are safe, though talks as though she were in the past, reminiscing on a day of snow. Daimon plays into it, suggesting they "build a snowman", but Victoria says that there is not enough time since their father will be home soon and will be angry if they are outside. She has a breakdown, and Ana tries to leave. The demon resumes control and warns Ana that "he" is back for the "[[Zoe Richards|only one to escape his trap]]". It says that it admires Victoria's stamina and reveals that Ana knows what the warning is about, causing her to tell Daimon that their father is back, despite Daimon's insistence that his body was cremated. The demon says that he has unfinished business.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:HastingsInOffice.png|thumb|250px|[[Louise Hastings]] listens]] [[Gabriella Rosetti]] and [[Louise Hastings]] are told what happened with Victoria Helstrom and the demon, and Rosetti points out that Victoria is still fighting. Hastings mentions a victim might have gotten away, but Ana insists she was the only one. When Daimon says the demon could be lying to cause conflict, Ana insists that their father is still out there. Rosetti and Hastings tell the siblings about [[Zoe Richards]], a girl who was tortured and nearly killed during the time of their father's killing spree, shortly before he died. Daimon and Hastings agree that it is worth looking into. Rosetti suggests warning Richards, but Ana instead suggests using her to lure their father out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Louise Hastings returns to her office from getting medicine. She puts it in her pocket and returns to her office, finding Caretaker inside. He asks why it feels like she is avoiding him, but Hastings dismisses him, saying that she needs to check in on Victoria Helstrom. Caretaker says that he would like to as well.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:GabriellaTalksAboutPast.png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] talks about her beliefs]] Daimon and Ana Helstrom and Gabriella Rosetti drive to Richards' house, and Rosetti asks what their plan is. Ana dismisses the conversation and says that they will figure it out. She comments that she cannot believe Rosetti is a nun, flirting with her, making her uncomfortable. Daimon cuts her off and comments that Ana often does not respect boundaries. Rosetti explains that nuns are typically just looking for refuge from the world, and that she was not fulfilled from her parties. Ana continues her flirting.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Caretaker says to Hastings that Victoria Helstrom is getting weaker while the demon gets stronger, suggesting that he take care of her. Hastings notes that Daimon has conservatorship over her and that it is not what is best for her, but Caretaker insists that they are simply putting off the inevitable.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*As they enter the secure ward, Hastings says that she shares Caretaker's concern and that she is handling Victoria Helstrom. Caretaker explains that [[Blood|people]] are scared of Daimon and Ana being together, which could cause problems. The demon opens the door panel from inside, letting Caretaker see her before suddenly slamming it again.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:AubreeOpensDoor.png|thumb|250px|[[Aubree Richards]] opens her door]] Rosetti and the Helstrom siblings arrive at the [[Richards Residence]]. Pretending to be her sister Zoe, [[Aubree Richards]] answers the door. Rosetti says that they are researching survivors of violent crime, asking to interview her. "Zoe Richards" expresses anger and closes the door in Rosetti's face. The real Zoe Richards realizes that Ana was involved in her [[Kidnapping of Zoe Richards|kidnapping]], and as the trio leave, Aubree waits for her sister to be out of sight and calls the trio back, letting them in. [[Magoth]], possessing Bryce, watches as they enter the house.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:KILLHIMScrabble.png|thumb|250px|[[Tooms]] is ordered to kill [[Caretaker]]]] Patient [[Tooms]] plays with the spinner on a board game in [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]]. The demon inside of Victoria Helstrom uses {{WPS|Scrabble}} pieces and the spinner to communicate with Tooms, instructing him to kill Caretaker.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*"Zoe Richards" places her gun on her table, saying that she always has one for protection. Rosetti apologizes for bringing up past trauma, and Ana Helstrom says that she is still haunted by her own experience. Rosetti asks about what happened, and Richards "recounts" the kidnapping. Ana, suddenly uncomfortable and remembering her father's victims, asks to use the bathroom and exits the room.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:AnaWalksUpStairs.png|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] sneaks around the house]] As "Zoe Richards" continues talking, Ana Helstrom goes upstairs and investigates a bedroom. Daimon follows her upstairs and asks what she is doing, prompting Ana to reply that she believes someone else is there. The two bicker, and Ana suggests that something is not right with "Zoe Richards".{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*"Zoe Richards" continues to talk about "her" experience, and Rosetti comforts her. They are interrupted when Ana Helstrom comes downstairs and asks for specific details, demanding to know what she is hiding. Helstrom accuses Richards of lying and grabs her arm, trying to find the truth, prompting Richards to kick them out. Richards grabs her gun and the trio leave.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Outside, [[Daimon Helstrom]] states they should have been honest with Richards, and Rosetti asks why Ana grabbed "her" arm. Daimon asks if she sensed anything, but Ana says she did not because she was not finished. Daimon explains to Rosetti that Ana can read people, and Ana insists that Richards could not have escaped, since she watched their father burn Zoe Richards alive. Ana walks off, upset at not being believed.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[Magoth]] approaches Zoe and Aubree Richards, offering them a chance to get revenge against Ana Helstrom. He asks Aubree to lead her into a trap, where [[Basar|someone strong enough]] will kill her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[Tooms]] watches [[Caretaker]] as he asks [[Louise Hastings]] when the Helstrom siblings will return, and she says she does not know. When he asks if she is hiding the truth from him again, Hastings says that she is going to lunch. Caretaker asks to join, and Hastings invites him to go to a [[El Cartel Food Truck|taco truck]] with him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:KtharaFloating.png|thumb|250px|[[Kthara]] floats]] The demon inside [[Victoria Helstrom]] telekinetically triggers the fire alarm, prompting an evacuation of the building. Hastings goes to check security and Caretaker goes to leave. Meanwhile, "Helstrom" levitates in her cell, muttering to herself.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*'''[[Attack on Caretaker]]''': As the building is evacuated, Tooms shoves Caretaker against a window and attempts to choke him. Caretaker fights back and Hastings rushes to help him, but gets pushed to the ground. Caretaker punches Tooms repeatedly and pushes him to the ground, after which he is taken by security guards.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Caretaker helps Hastings to her feet and asks if she is alright, and Hastings says that she is. He notices that she has dropped something, and, picking it up, sees that it is medicine. Hastings silently takes it back and walks away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[Ana Helstrom]] lays in her hotel room bed, remembering holding her father's [[Shard|knife]] while he tortured a victim. She remembers the demon inside her mother saying that her father would leave "no stone unturned".{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:GabandDaimAtDiner.png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] and [[Daimon Helstrom]] sit at a diner]] Daimon Helstrom and [[Gabriella Rosetti]] sit at a restaurant, and Helstrom says that they should have kept an eye on the [[Richards Residence]] rather than leave. Rosetti asks if he knew that his sister watched their father kill people, and he replies he suspected but never knew for a fact. He explains that Ana never wanted to talk about it, and Rosetti comforts him, stating that it is not his fault. She advises Daimon to show his sister empathy, but he suddenly realizes that Ana will be going back to the Richards Residence.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Ana Helstrom visits a dance club, looking for someone.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Hastings and Caretaker sit in Hastings' office, and she says that the patient who attacked him is not normally violent. Caretaker realizes that it is the result of manipulations from the demon inside Victoria Helstrom. He insists that Hastings talk about her condition, having deduced that it is cancer. She shares that it is lung cancer, and that Rosetti is intended to replace her. Caretaker shares his concerns for Hastings, and she acknowledges that she should have told him. She explains that only Caretaker and her doctor know and that she is refusing chemotherapy. Hastings says she only wants to get a taco with her friend.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:AnaTouchesPeople.png|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] walks through the club]] At the club, Ana Helstrom walks around and looks for "Zoe Richards", touching people to sense for any bad individuals. She arrives at a table, where a man gropes her, and she senses that he is a killer. The man, [[Jake (Jerk)|Jake]], introduces himself, and she pretends to flirt with him, preparing to take him outside. However, she spots "Zoe Richards" and walks away. Jake grabs her arm, prompting Helstrom to use her powers and stop his heart. She resumes following "Richards" as people check on Jake.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Rosetti and Daimon Helstrom arrive at the Richards Residence, and no one answers. The two enter the house and split up, with Helstrom going upstairs and calling for his sister. Helstrom finds the bedroom his sister investigated earlier, now a mess. Discovering another door, he enters and finds that it leads to another stairwell.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Rosetti finds a door herself and enters, finding that it leads down to the basement. She asks after [[Zoe Richards]] and finds a woman with a face covered with burn scars, who tells her, "I'm Zoe."{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Daimon Helstrom enters the room at the top of the stairs and finds pictures of Zoe and [[Aubree Richards]], realizing that they are identical twins and that the woman they met was in fact Zoe's sister.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:AubreeWalksAway.png|thumb|250px|[[Aubree Richards]] leads [[Ana Helstrom]] to a trap]] Ana Helstrom continues to follow "Zoe Richards", in fact Aubree, calling after her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Zoe Richards asks Rosetti where her sister is, threatening to burn the house down if Rosetti gets closer. Zoe explains that Aubree did not think the world would accept her, and that she realized that Ana Helstrom was the young girl involved in her [[Kidnapping of Zoe Richards|kidnapping]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Ana Helstrom continues to follow Aubree Richards into an alley, then a parking lot.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Rosetti realizes that Aubree Richards had been posing as Zoe, and Zoe tells her about Ana having tricked her into walking up to her [[Marduk Kurios|father]] and getting kidnapped and tortured.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Ana Helstrom wanders through the lot, looking for Aubree Richards.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:DaimonReasonsWithZoe.png|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] tries to reason with [[Zoe Richards]]]] Rosetti offers to help Zoe Richards, but Zoe refuses, saying that Aubree said the same thing. She claims that she is helping herself now and sets the basement alight. Daimon Helstrom hears Rosetti calling, explaining they are in the cellar, where Helstrom joins her. Rosetti tries to get through to Richards, but she says that this is the only way to end her guilt and pain, and that she should have died when she was kidnapped. The stairs to the basement burn down, but Rosetti convinces Richards to leave. Helstrom uses his telekinesis to break open the external door to the basement, and they rush out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Ana Helstrom continues to look for Aubree Richards, but hears a low growl nearby.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*As the fire department arrives at the Richards Residence, Zoe Richards tells Daimon Helstrom and Rosetti about a [[Magoth|college student]] who came after they left and offered the Richardses revenge on Ana. She tells them that Ana is being led into a trap and that [[Basar|someone]] will be there to kill her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Ana Helstrom finds Aubree Richards, who admits to her that she will finally be avenging her sister. The demon attacks Helstrom and calls her "Button", causing her to conclude it is her father. Helstrom throws a pole into her "father's" chest, but he simply pulls it out. They two begin to fight, and the demon throws her onto the ceiling repeatedly. He tosses her to the side and turns his attention to Richards.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:AubreeRichardsMurderedByBasar.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Aubree Richards]] is eaten]] Richards is suddenly frightened, insisting that she should be safe since she did what the demon asked. However, the demon takes off his sweatshirt, revealing a mouth in his stomach. Helstrom watches as her "father" begins to consume Richards through his stomach. She gets back up and when she sees Richards killed, leaps over the railing onto a dumpster two stories down. Helstrom recovers and crawls away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*The demon finishes eating Richards and turns toward where Helstrom had been, grinning.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Ana Helstrom walks away and stumbles from her injuries. Daimon and Rosetti arrive, and Daimon goes to Ana. Ana says that she is certain it was their father and that he was very strong. Daimon comforts her and says that he believes her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*[[File:HastingsEatingTaco.png|thumb|250px|[[Louise Hastings]] and [[Caretaker]] eat tacos]] Visiting the [[El Cartel Food Truck]], Hastings insists that Caretaker give Rosetti a chance. Caretaker insists that Hastings is irreplaceable, and that the established history between them and the Helstroms is too important to walk away from. Hastings says that she is tired, but Caretaker offers to help her. He explains that their job is not done and people are going to get hurt. He says that there are other forces at play, and that the world cannot cope with a Helstrom family reunion.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*Daimon Helstrom helps Ana into his car.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}
*"Victoria Helstrom" sits in her room and smiles.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS103}}

====20th====
*[[Gabriella Rosetti]] plants seeds and works with several gardeners.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[Ellis]] checks on [[Kthara]] and sees that she is alright.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[Ana Helstrom]] puts on a record and listens to it at [[Daimon Helstrom]]'s [[Daimon Helstrom's House|house]]. She looks through the fridge and several cabinets. She finds bread and puts it in the toaster. She opens a jar of peanut butter and puts some on her finger, tasting it.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Daimon Helstrom goes jogging.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[Caretaker]] returns to his van after buying donuts from [[Gary & Roy's Doughnuts]]. He puts them in the back of the van and closes the door.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[Louise Hastings]] struggles to open her medicine bottle. She gets frustrated and throws the bottle against her window. The bottle falls to the floor, now open, and Hastings rests on the sink, upset at her worsening condition.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Rosetti approaches a gardener and compliments her work. She receives a call, but ignores it.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana walks through Daimon's house, exploring.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Daimon continues jogging.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana picks up a framed photograph of her and Daimon, when she hears a knock on the door. She turns off the music and answers it, seeing Rosetti, teasingly guessing that she is there for Daimon. Rosetti says that he called, and Ana expresses disappointment, flirtatiously saying that she could do better. Rosetti expresses condolences over Ana being attacked and says that she is there to help. Ana turns around as Hastings arrives and expresses disappointment. Her toast pops out of the toaster, burnt.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:RosettiMeetsAna.png|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] lets [[Gabriella Rosetti]] in]] Rosetti compliments Daimon's house, while Ana stares out the window. Ana comments that they took their mother's money, and Daimon explains that Ana means the family trust was split between the two of them. Caretaker arrives and greets the Helstrom family, offering them donuts. Hastings introduces him to Rosetti.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Daimon starts a formal meeting, saying that he and Ana have reason to believe their [[Marduk Kurios|father]] is back in a new form. Daimon explains that he is marking people for possession and targeting them. Ana asks how to kill him, and Caretaker says that they cannot without a [[Keeper Demons|Keeper demon]]. Daimon asks where to find one, but Caretaker explains that the [[Keeper's Skull|skull]] they found could contain the demon.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Caretaker attempts to continue explaining, but Ana gets up and begins to leave, explaining that the skull is in [[San Francisco]]. She leaves the house and attempts to call [[Chris Yen]], who does not answer. Daimon rushes out and says that he can drive them to the airport, insisting on going with her despite Ana's protests. Ana scolds Daimon for involving the others and explains that "their father" would kill them easily. Daimon insists on helping her and says that he loves San Francisco, making Ana laugh.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Rosetti expresses confusion at the Helstrom father being alive, since people do not come back from the dead. Caretaker mentions that {{WPS|Jesus}} did just that, and Rosetti says that a soul could not simply be contained, but Caretaker says that he and Hastings have done it. Rosetti argues that it is immoral, and Hastings agrees. Caretaker describes the Helstrom father as a monster and pure evil, and that his soul is dead. Rosetti asks what Caretaker's claims say about his children.
*Rosetti goes to a church and lights several candles, praying. She does the sign of the cross and walks away as the candles are blown out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:RaumReachesForRosetti.png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] is attacked by [[Raum]]]] Rosetti goes to confession with whom she believes to be Father [[Joshua Crow]], unaware that Crow has been possessed by [[Raum]]. She says that she is meant to report to the [[Terrazi|archbishop]] if she finds any disturbing behavior from the Helstrom family, but that it is complicated. She talks about how the church tells its followers that faith is their strength, but that sometimes life tests faith through their experiences and feelings. She talks about how she is feeling doubts, wondering who she is to pass judgement.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Raum breathes heavily and asks if there was a sin anywhere in what Rosetti said, asking if she has had any lustful thoughts. Rosetti says that she is not sure and that everyone has had such thoughts. Raum asks if she likes the way he makes her feel in a sexual manner, offering to make her feel the same. Rosetti realizes what is happening and tries to leave the booth, finding the door stuck. Raum calls her a fighter and says that it had been centuries since he attacked someone like her. He shoves his hand through the window of the booth, and Rosetti gasps.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:RaumDefeated.png|thumb|250px|[[Caretaker]] places a [[Keeper Talisman]] on [[Raum]]'s head]] Rosetti begins chanting in Latin at the demon, who flies backward and out of the confessional. Caretaker fights Raum as Rosetti watches, and puts a [[Keeper Talisman]] on him. Rosetti asks if he followed her, and Caretaker explains that he needed to know he could trust her. Caretaker says that there is something Rosetti needs to see.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana and Daimon Helstrom arrive at Ana's [[Ana Helstrom's Auction House|auction house]], and Daimon comments that he never imagined she would be an art fan due to her own lack of ability, but Ana says that making art is not a prerequisite for selling it. Ana says that she deals in antiquities. Helstrom continues to be sarcastic, and the pair banter. Ana calls after [[Chris Yen]] and checks to see if he texted her back. Daimon asks how much a sword is worth, and expresses shock when Ana says it is worth over three million dollars.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana and Daimon continue to look for Yen and find a file knocked over. Ana realizes that Yen is not there and the alarm was not set when they entered. Ana enters their vault, noticing blood on the handle. The siblings explore and find the corpse of [[Cameron Tate]], and Ana realizes that the [[Keeper's Skull]] is gone, saying that they need to find Yen.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Yen arrives at a playground, carrying the skull in a bag. He finds a door leading into the sewer system and uses a rock to break the door open. He rubs his hands as he enters the underground area.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Rosetti and Caretaker arrive at the [[Blood Hotel]], and Rosetti asks if the Keeper Talisman exorcised Raum. Caretaker explains that it is made from the remains of a Keeper demon, and explains that they rebelled against their own kind. [[Finn Miller]] greets them and tells him in code that they have a demon to hold and that Rosetti is with him. Rosetti figures out that it is not a regular hotel.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Several members of the [[Blood]] go to Caretaker's truck and begin loosening Raum's restraints to bring him into the hotel.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana Helstrom kneels over Tate's body and looks through his wallet for identification. Ana denies knowing him to Daimon Helstrom and uses her abilities to see the history of the axe sticking out of him. Daimon asks what she saw and Ana says that it was a robbery of some kind. Daimon suggests they check the security camera.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:TateDead.png|thumb|250px|[[Cameron Tate]] is found dead]] Daimon and Ana watch the security footage of Yen brutally murdering Tate, and Ana attempts to defend him, upsetting Daimon. Ana watches as Yen leaves with the skull, wondering why he would take it. Daimon focuses on the murder and suggests calling the police, but Ana says that they need to focus on their father, who is growing more powerful. Ana suggests staying on track, and Daimon asks if she feels nothing for the murder victim. Ana says that he was disgusting, like his [[Edward Tate|brother]], causing Daimon to realize she did know him. Ana asks for help cleaning up, but no lecturing. Daimon tries to lecture anyway, and Ana tells him to leave. Hesitantly, Daimon agrees to help.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[Louise Hastings]] enters the secure ward of [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]], and [[Ellis]] tells her that it has been smooth, and even [[Kthara]] has been quiet. Hastings gets concerned about this and approaches her room, seeing her passed out. Hastings asks if she was sedated for blood work, confusing Ellis, who swears she was fine that morning. Hastings realizes that she is deteriorating, and decides to take her outside.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Rosetti walks through the Blood Hotel and sees several patients being kept comatose. She asks who they are, and Caretaker explains that they are possessed. Raum is brought through, and Rosetti follows as he is brought into a room of his own. Caretaker explains that the Blood run it and have been fighting and containing demons for centuries, putting them in comas to prevent the people from suffering while stranding the monster inside its host. Caretaker explains that he is a member of the Blood, and that the patients are kept sedated forever.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:TateSnapped.png|thumb|250px|[[Cameron Tate]]'s body is folded]] Ana Helstrom folds Tate's body using her telekinesis, and Daimon comments that she has gotten stronger. Daimon asks if she has ever talked to anyone about what happened after their [[Marduk Kurios|father]] [[Kidnapping of Ana Helstrom|kidnapped]] her, and notices that she does not seem phased by Tate's death. Ana demands that he continues cleaning and stops talking, saying that the sooner they finish the sooner they can return to their [[Victoria Helstrom|mother]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Hastings takes Kthara outside, and comments on her lack of ability to feel the sun and the air. She asks how this affects Kthara, who says that memory is a powerful thing, remembering the feelings. She says that the thought of it calms her. Hastings asks when she last felt that, causing Kthara to become sentimental and say it has been a long time.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Kthara says that she was with someone and in love, eating strawberries with them and their children. Hastings asks if she is referring to the Helstrom children, which Kthara denies, saying that they are Victoria Helstrom's children, not hers. Kthara goes on to describe her children lovingly and talk about how they used to hug her and sleep on her breast, and how she loved them until they were taken from her. Hastings asks who took them, but Kthara says that some memories are too painful and that she prefers to think of the sun.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Hastings notices that something is different about Kthara, and Kthara talks about how while death is a release, there is nothing like being alive. Hastings asks who she is, and Kthara gives Hastings her name, saying that she is just like Hastings, a woman betrayed by what she held dear. Kthara realizes in the sun.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana suggests getting a cooler to dispose of Tate's body, when she hears a rattling from someone at the auction house. Daimon goes to see who it is, and finds Officer [[Derrick Jackson]] with the [[San Francisco Police Department]], who asks who Daimon is. Daimon responds sarcastically and introduces himself, and Jackson asks where his boyfriend, [[Chris Yen]], is and expresses his belief that Yen is cheating on Jackson with Daimon. Jackson asks where Yen is, and Helstrom faces Ana.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Yen continues to wander through the sewers and finds his feet covered in spiders. He kicks them off and sits down underneath [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]], placing the [[Keeper's Skull]] in front of him as he comments on not liking the location.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Jackson demands to know what kind of operation requires Yen's long hours, and says that she treats Yen poorly. Ana apologizes and says that she is taking responsibility, satisfying Jackson. Ana lies to Jackson, claiming that he was sent on a last minute appraisal overseas, saying that he will be home soon. Jackson notices blood on her shirt, and Ana claims it came from Daimon dropping an antique weapon. Jackson threatens to break up with Yen if Ana is not less demanding and leaves. Daimon compliments Ana's ability to lie, and Ana suggests that Yen needs a better boyfriend. Ana walks back to the vault, and Daimon looks at her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana mops the floor where Tate was killed, and Daimon asks what Yen does for her. Ana says they buy and sell artifacts, but Daimon does not believe her. Daimon says that she is defensive, and Ana says that what they do is not his business. Daimon asks what Ana would have done if Jackson did not believe her lies, and says that he knows she is lying. He says that he wants to hear her say it, and Ana confesses that Yen helps her kill people. Ana asks if Daimon is satisfied, causing a tense moment between them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:Finn Miller.png|thumb|250px|[[Finn Miller]] talks to [[Caretaker]]]] [[Finn Miller]] asks if [[Esther Smith]] knows what Caretaker is doing, and Caretaker says that he does not answer to her. Miller says that how the hotel runs is his call, but Caretaker says that that could change. Rosetti reads the files of several patients to Caretaker, saying that they had families and Daimon Helstrom can save them. Caretaker explains that that results in the demon being set free, plotting to kill. Rosetti says that putting people in comas is not the answer, but Caretaker explains that exorcisms are not the answer either. Rosetti goes to check on [[Joshua Crow]], and Miller and Caretaker glare at each other.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana Helstrom explains that Tate helped his brother murder women and were rich enough to buy their way out of getting caught. She explains that she is careful and makes sure that every person she kills deserves it. Daimon says that she is not correcting anything, but gets cut off by Ana. Daimon continues to say that she does not want it to be true that she is capable of killing.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana says that anyone is capable of killing, but Daimon says that their bloodline makes it different, saying that she kills for her own benefit, causing Ana to think that Daimon is comparing her to her father. Ana insists that it is different, since the people he kills are like him, but Daimon explains that her logic gives others the right to kill her. Ana simply expresses confidence that they would fail.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:KeeperSkullBitingYen.png|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] is bitten by the [[Keeper's Skull]]]] Yen makes the Keeper's Skull bite down on his arm and chews the skeleton of a spider. He suddenly spits it out, saying that it is not okay for the skull to make him do that.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Kthara is brought back to her room and senses a force hurting her. She stops the wheelchair and refuses to go back in there, demanding to know what was changed. Hastings insists that nothing has changed, and Kthara asks if it was Caretaker who changed it. Kthara continues to refuse to enter her room, and Hastings asks what is wrong. Kthara confesses to giving Hastings cancer and offers to take it away if Hastings removes what changed in her room. Two security guards pick up Kthara's wheelchair and carry her in her room as she screams.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana Helstrom looks through a box of things given to her by her father from his killings. Daimon Helstrom asks her to talk to him, and she says that she does not take pleasure from her father's gifts, but pain. She says that she uses the pain to stop people who spread it, suggesting she would be a bad person if she did not.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana explains that the box was a gift from her mother, and that she started using it to hold her father's gifts. She explains that she did not know where the gifts came from, she just thought it was his way of showing that he loved her. She explained that their mother hated the gifts, and that she thought it meant she hated Ana. Daimon assures her that she did not hate Ana, and Ana says that she knows.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana explains that when she and her brother went to clean out their [[Helstrom Residence|childhood home]], she found the box in their basement, which she had never gotten rid of, suggesting it made her mother weak. Daimon asks if she ever thought of trying to return the items to the victims' families, but Ana points out that people do not want to learn that their loved one was killed by a serial killer, resolving to bury the box with their father after she kills him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:Crow RaumPleads.png|thumb|250px|[[Joshua Crow]] pleads for help]] Rosetti sees Raum burn through his Keeper Talisman and attack a nurse. Miller and other Blood members restrain him as Raum calls out to Rosetti for help. Caretaker pulls Rosetti out of the room and says that he is not happy with it either, but that they cannot stop it, saying that Rosetti can still leave the fight. Caretaker explains that he cannot run from the fight, despite having tried. Rosetti asks if Hastings knows, and Caretaker does not answer, causing Rosetti to leave.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana and Daimon look at the box Tate is in, and Daimon asks how she normally disposes of bodies. Ana says she does not know, and suggests dumping it in the bay, which Daimon says is too risky. Daimon says that there is another way and uses his demonic abilities to light Tate's body on fire. He falls over, and Ana rushes to his aid. The two share a look with each other.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Hastings works with a patient and struggles to write notes. She compliments the patient's progress, and Rosetti enters and asks to talk to Hastings. Rosetti asks what Hastings knows about the Blood, and Hastings says that it is out of their control. Rosetti asks why she is defending them, and Hastings says that she does not agree with their actions. Rosetti points out her obligation to report the incident, and Hastings says that the Church already knows about it. Rosetti becomes upset about Hastings' dismissal of the church, but Hastings says that they did.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:Moon in Helstrom 1x4.png|thumb|250px|[[Louise Hastings]] talks to [[Gabriella Rosetti]]]] Hastings says that she still finds her strength from faith, but that her faith is in people. Rosetti says that they cannot simply allow the people in Blood hotels to die, and Hastings says that saving them results in the demon hurting someone else. She asks what Rosetti thinks the answer is, explaining that the situation is not simple. She says that demons are the only enemy, asking Rosetti to remember that.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Ana and Daimon Helstrom return to [[Portland]], and Ana declares her intention to return to her [[The Nines Hotel|hotel]]. Daimon asks where she thinks Chris Yen went, and Helstrom replies that she does not know, and that it is not like him to disappear. Daimon again offers to let Ana stay at his house, saying that they would do alright for themselves together, and Ana turns him down. Ana gets in a car she called for and drives away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Daimon Helstrom returns home and senses someone there. He finds [[Magoth]], eating donuts and teasing him. Magoth asks Helstrom if he spoke to his sister, and deduces that she told Helstrom the truth. Magoth offers to make a deal, trading his sister. Daimon asks what his father needs her for, and Magoth refuses, so Daimon tells him to tell his father to talk to Helstrom himself. Magoth offers Helstrom's sister in exchange for his mother, and Helstrom responds by attacking him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Magoth responds by telekinetically throwing a fire poker at Helstrom, which Helstrom blocks using a table, which he then throws at Magoth. Magoth pushes a bookshelf on top of Helstrom and jumps on top of it. [[Ana Helstrom]] shows up and pushes Magoth over, lifting the bookshelf off of Daimon.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*[[File:Ana&DaimonDefeatMagoth.png|thumb|250px|[[Bryce (Student)|Bryce]] is exorcised]] Ana punches Magoth several times and the two fight, as she begins to kill Magoth, holding him in place. Daimon rushes up behind him and exorcises the demon, freeing [[Bryce (Student)|Bryce]], who thanks Helstrom before passing out. Ana compliments Daimon's abilities and says that her hotel room was not available, so she thought she would stay with him to save money. Daimon points out that she could afford the room if she wanted and asks help cleaning up, but Ana refuses to clean and walks away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Kthara screams in pain and bangs against the wall of her room, writhing.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Underneath Kthara's room, Yen drinks a bottle of alcohol as he stares at the Keeper's Skull, seeing an eye appear in its hole.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS104}}
*Stuck inside her own head, [[Victoria Helstrom]] relives the memory of being committed to [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]] repeatedly. Cracks start to appear in the ceiling of her room within the memory.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Daimon Helstrom and Bryce agree that it is best if the pair does not talk to each other. Helstrom tells Bryce to lie to the police about his experiences.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Bryce tries to go to sleep, but sees horrors when he closes his eyes.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
{{DubiousSectionEnd}}

====21st====
*[[Riri Williams]] fixes a few trucks for the Head of Sanitation for the city of [[Cambridge]], [[Massachusetts]]. In exchange, he allows her to work out of a [[Cambridge Department of Public Works Garage]].{{Ref|BPWF}}<ref>In ''[[Black Panther: Wakanda Forever]]'', Riri Williams says that she got access to the garage where she built her vibranium detector and stored her armor after making a deal with the head of sanitation. Williams started attending MIT in September 2020 (see other references), shortly after the shooting that killed Gary Williams and Natalie Washington on July 24, 2020 (see other references). In ''[[Karma's a Glitch]]'', Williams tells her mother that she began building her Ironheart armors as a reaction to the shooting. In ''Black Panther: Wakanda Forever'', she says she spent "two years" building her first suit. Since she has spent most of her time since the shooting at MIT, she likely had access to the garage for those two years she spent building her suit. It can be estimated that she made her deal with the head of sanitation sometime during her first semester at college. The Fall 2020 semester at MIT lasted between [https://facultygovernance.mit.edu/sites/default/files/Fall_2020_Emergency_Academic_Regulations_and_Policies_FULL_FINAL.pdf September 1 and December 9, 2020], so this event can be placed at the midpoint, October 21, 2020. </ref>

====22nd====
*"Salka" by [[Hassan Shakosh]], featuring [[Wegz]] is released.{{Ref|RealEvents}}{{Ref|MK103}}
{{DubiousSection}}
*[[File:Burnt Frat House.png|thumb|250px|Burnt down [[Phi Gamma Epsilon House]]]][[Daimon Helstrom]] drives past the [[Phi Gamma Epsilon]] [[Phi Gamma Epsilon House|house]] near his [[Gateway University|university]], seeing it after being burned down. He slows down as he passes it and notices students standing near a shrine set up outside of the house. He drives away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Helstrom arrives at his office and puts his bag down. He puts books on his bookshelf as [[Bryce (Student)|Bryce]] enters and asks for him, startling him. Helstrom asks why he is there, and Bryce says that he has been struggling to process being possessed and the deaths of everyone else in his [[Phi Gamma Epsilon|fraternity]]. Bryce asks if he killed his brothers, but Helstrom assures him that it was not his fault.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Bryce suggests dropping out of school but Helstrom encourages him not to, stating that he will have someone call him. Bryce asks what good it would do since he would be locked away, pointing out that it is why Helstrom had Bryce lie to the police. Bryce comments on him being an ethics professor giving morally impermissible advice and starts to leave. Helstrom attempts to stop Bryce, and Bryce cuts him off, saying that he could not eat or sleep since the previous night. He talks about the horrors he has seen, and Helstrom says that he cannot imagine what he is experiencing. Bryce comments that that is obvious and walks out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[Ana Helstrom]] wakes up from a dream in which she was buried alive, and finds herself having imagined dirt on the bed. She becomes startled and falls out of bed, swearing to herself.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Daimon Helstrom calls [[Gabriella Rosetti]], who goes to his university. Helstrom asks Rosetti to talk to Bryce, and Rosetti asks if Helstrom ever wonders how the other people Helstrom has saved feel similarly. Helstrom explains that [[Louise Hastings]] usually does that part, but that Rosetti needs experience and suggests that he should not be the one to handle it. Rosetti confesses that Helstrom is right, and Helstrom teases her. Helstrom notices that Rosetti is upset and asks if she is alright, but Rosetti says that she is and takes Bryce's information. She walks away, and Helstrom looks after her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[File:SickVictoria.png|thumb|250px|[[Kthara]] scratches at the floor]] Hastings looks into [[Kthara]]'s room at [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]] and tells her to wake up. She finds Kthara asleep on the floor, so she has a guard unlock the door. Hastings prepares a sedative and approaches Kthara, but finds her unconscious. Hastings tells the guard to get help. While he rushes out, Hastings notices Kthara scratching at the floor of her room.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[Victoria Helstrom]] continues reliving the memory of getting committed to Saint Teresa's. However, the memory gets cut off as she notices a peeled wallpaper. She hears a knock on the door and rushes to answer it, finding a young "[[Kthara|Ana Helstrom]]." Victoria embraces her "daughter."{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[File:AnaReturnsHome.png|thumb|250px|"[[Kthara|Ana]]" returns home]] Hastings calls Daimon Helstrom and tells him what is happening. Daimon arrives and approaches his mother's room, sensing a strange presence. He proceeds to call Ana, interrupting her having sex, and asks her to come to the hospital since it is an emergency.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Ana arrives and asks what the emergency is, and Daimon tells her what happened with their mother. He tells her that she is in a coma for unknown reasons. Ana looks into Kthara's room and senses the [[Keeper's Skull]]. She recognizes the presence, and Daimon realizes that [[Chris Yen]] is somewhere at the hospital. Ana again looks into the room.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Inside her false memory, Victoria offers food to "Ana" and asks her what happened, while Daimon looks on nervously. Victoria asks how "Ana" got away, and "Ana" says that she hit her [[Marduk Kurios|father]] and ran. Lightning strikes, and "Ana" counts until the thunder comes. Daimon comments that "Ana's" story does not make sense, but Victoria asks him not. Daimon presses, and "Ana" again counts to the thunder. Daimon yells at "Ana," and Victoria scolds Daimon, and thunder strikes again. "Ana" sees a [[Keeper|figure]] out the window, frightening her, and begs her mom to protect her. Victoria pulls back the curtain and promises "Ana" that she won't get hurt, when another lightning strike causes the power to go out, and "Ana" says that the figure is coming.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[Caretaker]] enters the security room after checking the perimeter of the hospital, saying that he could not find Yen. Hastings reports that security footage shows that he never entered the building. Daimon asks why he would come, and Ana says it was manipulating him. Hastings asks what the skull wants, and Caretaker suggests that it wants to contain evil. When Daimon says that it should only work on his father, Caretaker explains that since Victoria was marked by their father, the Keeper would contain Kthara as well. Caretaker explains that the closer the skull gets, the worse Victoria's condition will be.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Daimon expresses urgency in finding Yen, and Hastings comes to a realization. She leads Daimon and Ana into Kthara's room and shows them that Kthara was digging, and they realize that Yen was underground. Daimon asks how to get there.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[File:DemonCatchers.png|thumb|250px|Everyone discussing [[Chris Yen]]]] Daimon, Ana, and Caretaker enter the sewer system, and Ana asks if Yen will be okay when the skull is done with him, and Caretaker says that it depends on what is left of him. Ana responds with sarcasm, and Daimon asks what they are dealing with. Ana says the effects are bad due to it convincing Yen to go through the dirty area. Daimon tries to ask Caretaker not to go with them, suggesting he has an ulterior motive. Caretaker suggests that Ana cares more about Yen than Daimon or Victoria, and insists on going.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Rosetti finds Bryce and introduces herself, and Bryce asks if she is a psychologist. Rosetti explains that she is a novitiate, and Bryce turns away. Rosetti insists that she can help and says that he was not the first person possessed by [[Magoth]]. Bryce realizes that Magoth is still out there, and Rosetti says that Bryce is not alone. Bryce insists that she does not understand, and Rosetti asks him to help her stop it from happening again.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Hastings looks over Kthara, whose eyes flutter open.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*In her false memory, Victoria lights a candle as "Ana" sits on her lap. Victoria tells "Ana" about her experiences in storms as a young girl, and Daimon explains what thunder is after Victoria gives a more comforting explanation. Victoria tries to say that his version is less comforting, but Daimon insists that the truth is more important. Lightning strikes again and Victoria comforts "Ana," when the family hears a sound. Daimon goes to check the circuit breaker, prompting Victoria to again scold him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[File:GlassShattersOntoHelstroms.png|thumb|250px|The glass shatters onto the family]] Victoria hears a loud pounding on the door and shines a flashlight around the room. She sees a ghostly figure where "Ana" was standing and quickly moves the flashlight back, seeing "Ana" again, who says that she cannot see. The pounding continues from the door, and Victoria brings children in close. The pounding suddenly stops, and the windows shatter, frightening the family.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*In the real world, Victoria's body seizes momentarily before relaxing. Hastings wonders what is happening.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*In her false memory, Victoria notices that Daimon is missing and asks "Ana" where he is. She calls after her son and "Ana" takes her hand. Victoria rushes to the stairwell and looks up the stairs.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Ana Helstrom looks through the sewers for Yen, followed by Daimon, who suggests that they destroy it. Ana says it is a bad idea to destroy their only weapon against their father, and Caretaker agrees. Daimon suggests that Caretaker only agrees because of a benefit to him, but Caretaker explains that they would all benefit. Ana finds stuff of Yen's, and Daimon looks through it while Ana sees Yen and goes after her. Caretaker notices that Yen has been biting into rats. Daimon turns around and sees Ana missing, calling after her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*In her false memory, Victoria is led into Ana's room by her "daughter," thinking that Daimon was inside. "Ana" suggests playing a game, but Victoria insists on looking for Daimon. "Ana" says that Victoria needs to protect her, since she let her father [[Kidnapping of Ana Helstrom|kidnap]] her, and tries to guilt her. Victoria tells her to be quiet, and "Ana" comments on her journal, which Ana would not have known about, prompting Victoria to realize that she is not talking to Ana.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Victoria hears another pounding, and "Ana" reveals herself to truly be Kthara.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[File:Bryce'sMarking.png|thumb|250px|[[Bryce (Student)|Bryce]]'s marking]] Bryce sits irritably with Rosetti and talks to her about how he never believed that [[demons]] were real. Rosetti asks if Bryce knew what was happening, but Bryce says that he did not. Bryce explains that while he might have seen the demon, he definitely felt the demon. Rosetti asks if they communicated, which Bryce says he did not. Rosetti prepares to ask another question, but Bryce declares that he does not know, clearly upset.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Rosetti apologizes and says that she wants to understand. Bryce explains that the demon made him relive the moment where he was at his worst repeatedly, and that nothing he could do would change the result. Rosetti attempts to comfort him, but Bryce says that it was torture. Reflecting on the status of [[Joshua Crow]], Rosetti expresses little doubt about his emotions. Rosetti empathizes with him and assures him that he will be alright, saying that she and Daimon Helstrom will not let anything happen to her again. Bryce asks if she is sure, and Rosetti hesitates.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*'''[[Search for the Keeper's Skull]]''':
**In her false memory, Victoria Helstrom realizes what [[Kthara]] was doing to her. Kthara introduces herself and explains that she thought that appearing as [[Ana Helstrom]] would encourage Victoria to help her. Kthara explains that the pair need to help each other, since Kthara needs protection from Victoria's [[Marduk Kurios|husband]] putting them both in danger. Kthara says that she is also being punished by being in Victoria's mind and that time is running out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**More damage is caused to the house in Victoria Helstrom's memory, which Kthara explains as her husband trying to break her. Helstrom asks what to do, and Kthara asks for help with her plan. Helstrom asks why she should help, and Kthara says that getting back to their children is what matters and that if they survive, they will no longer be prisoners. The door opens and Kthara runs, saying it is no longer safe where they are. Helstrom goes with her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**[[File:CaretakerAndDaimon.png|thumb|250px|[[Caretaker]] and [[Daimon Helstrom]] argue]]Daimon Helstrom calls out for his sister, commenting about how she left after saying they should stick together. He asks if [[Caretaker]] tires of cleaning after, and Caretaker sympathizes with Helstrom having to deal with his mother. He asks how long Helstrom intends to care for her, and Helstrom simply replies that he will do it for as long as it takes. Caretaker asks how long his mother can, upsetting Helstrom.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Helstrom insists that Caretaker speaks plainly, and Caretaker says that there are other ways to help his mother without her suffering. He explains that destroying the skull will not save her, but rather put more people at risk. He also explains that exorcising his mother would be akin to sacrificing a war to win a single battle. Helstrom asks whether the [[Blood]] would really help the family they had been trying to kill, but Caretaker reminds him that he and Hastings had been protecting them. However, Helstrom says that if Caretaker had been protecting them, they would not be in their present situation.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In her false memory, Victoria Helstrom runs down the stairs of her house with Kthara.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In the real world, Helstrom's eyes move under her eyelids.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In her false memory, Helstrom sees a picture frame fall as the wallpaper beneath it is torn down and gets startled.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Helstrom's vitals spike, and [[Louise Hastings]] reports this. her eyes continue to move under her eyelids.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In her false memory, the door to her house flings open as Helstrom sees her "[[Keeper|husband]]". Kthara grabs Helstrom's hands and pulls her along as Helstrom's "husband" enters the house.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**[[File:YenFound.png|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] is found]] Ana Helstrom rushes through the sewers and wonders aloud how much longer she will be looking. She hears Yen gasp for air and finds him allowing the skull to bite down on his arm. Helstrom speaks gently to Yen and asks what he is doing, commenting on his state and the state of his shoes. Helstrom says that he is not himself, but Yen adds that she does not know who he is. Helstrom attempts to approach him, but Yen yells to stay away, startling her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Helstrom says that they can end the skull's influence and return to normal, but Yen suggests that "normal" simply means being Helstrom's errand boy. Helstrom is confused as Daimon Helstrom and joins.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Ana tells Daimon to back off and attempts to get through to Yen, saying that she did not want to lie to him, apologizing. Ana says that her father is coming and that the skull is the only thing that can stop him, saying that the situation would end sooner if he handed the skull over, offering to take him out in exchange. Yen says that he cannot, since he now has a job and is needed by the skull and not by Ana. Ana assures him that he does need him, but threatens to hurt Yen to get the skull.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Yen refuses and Daimon approaches Yen, but Ana throws him against a wall, prompting Daimon to retaliate. Daimon says that he will not let Yen hurt their mother, but Ana says that she will not let Daimon hurt Yen. She insists Yen will listen to her, but Daimon refuses to back off while rattling the pipes above them. Daimon says that their mom is dying, but Ana claims it is not their mother, as Caretaker arrives behind them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Ana asks why Daimon cannot let his mother go, and Daimon exclaims that it was his fault she was committed. The pipes fall, and Caretaker pushes the siblings out of the way in time to stop it. Ana notices that Yen is missing.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**[[File:KtharaCloseUp.png|thumb|250px|[[Kthara]] talks to [[Victoria Helstrom]]]] In her mind, Victoria Helstrom rushes into the basement of her house with Kthara, who locks the door. Helstrom sees her son bleeding out, but Kthara asks her to ignore the false moment as she sees her daughter getting taken away. Kthara says that she cannot change what happened, but Helstrom cries, saying that she could have done something.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Kthara tells Helstrom to hide while Helstrom continues to panic, declaring that she should have seen what her husband was. Kthara spins Helstrom around and begs for help, saying that they have to be strong. Helstrom asks why Kthara would need her help, since Kthara had controlled her head for so long. Helstrom realizes that Kthara is weak and only cares about herself. She explains that a real mother sacrifices for her children and that her husband is not chasing them, but rather something Kthara is frightened of and cannot control.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Kthara demands that Helstrom do what she asks, but Helstrom pushes Kthara against a wall with her mind. She says that while she did not do anything for her daughter, she can do something now and free herself from her burden. She rushes to the door while Kthara begs her not to. Helstrom declares that if she dies, Kthara would also die, and opens the door.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**[[File:TheKeeperWalksTowardsKthara.png|thumb|250px|The [[Keeper]] walks towards [[Kthara]]]] The [[Keeper]] walks down the stairs and passes Helstrom, approaching Kthara.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Daimon Helstrom, Ana Helstrom, and Caretaker rush through the sewers and come to a dead end, but Caretaker notices a ladder. Ana swears.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Victoria's body seizes as Hastings says that she is going into tachycardia.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Victoria rushes through the house in her mind and grabs at her heart as she dies.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**[[File:Hel 105-0258r.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Victoria Helstrom]] flatlines]] Hastings yells at Victoria to stay with her. Victoria hears the yell in her mind and follows the source of the noise. She sees a hospital bed and rushes to open the door to her house, seeing her hospital room, causing her to panic.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Yen sneaks through the hospital and enters the secure ward by following doctors carrying a medical machine, with the skull in his hand under a cover. He sees Victoria struggling and uncovers the skull. Daimon and Ana arrive as Daimon telekinetically throws Yen against the wall, causing him to drop the skull.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Daimon rushes to see Victoria convulsing while Ana checks on Yen. Staring from down the hallway, Daimon kneels over the skull and tries to use his demonic abilities to break it. The skull rumbles.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Victoria's body continues convulsing as doctors struggle to treat her and she flatlines.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In her mind, Victoria struggles to right herself. She rushes over to a wall and tears down the wallpaper.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**As her body shakes, Victoria lifts a finger in the real world.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In her mind, Victoria tears down more wallpaper and sees the door to her hospital room.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In the real world, Victoria's body convulses.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**In her mind, Victoria cries into the window on the door.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**[[File:KeeperSkullCracks.png|thumb|250px|The [[Keeper's Skull]] cracks]] In the real world, Victoria's body continues convulsing. The skull continues to shake as Daimon attempts to destroy it. Ana rushes over to Daimon as the skull fractures, but Victoria suddenly wakes up and screams for Daimon to stop.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
**Daimon and Ana look up at their mother, who breathes heavily. Daimon asks after his mother as Ana expresses shock.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Victoria sits in a wheelchair with the skull in her lap and Daimon and Ana next to her. Victoria tells her children that Kthara is terrified of the Keeper, which weakened her and took control. Victoria says that she does not know how or how long it will last, but Daimon says that the only thing that matters is that Victoria is back.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Victoria turns to her daughter and reveals to her that Kthara used her against Victoria, and comments that both her children had grown, and that she never thought she would see them again. Ana walks away, and Daimon and Victoria look after her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[File:YenLooksOutSlot.png|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] locked in a cell]]Ana Helstrom watches as Yen paces in his room in the hospital and scratches at his now bandaged arms, saying that he and the skull need each other. Yen notices Helstrom and rushes to his door, asking for the skull. Hastings assures Helstrom that staying there is best for Yen, and Caretaker explains that it will take time for the skull's effects to wear off. Yen says that the skull needs him. Helstrom sarcastically expresses relief that her mother is saved yet Yen was scarred.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[Gabriella Rosetti]] looks at a missing poster for [[Joshua Crow]] and remembers the pain he appeared to be in at the [[Blood Hotel]]. Daimon Helstrom goes to her office and asks how her conversation with [[Bryce (Student)|Bryce]] went, and Rosetti says that formerly possessed people need more help than they realized and to talk about their experiences. Rosetti says that there is more than Helstrom knows, and Helstrom reveals that his mother is back. Rosetti describes it as a miracle, and Helstrom says that it is a start.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Rosetti feels guilty and says she needs to show Helstrom something. Helstrom asks for it to happen later, but Rosetti insists on its importance.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*[[File:RosettiSearchesCrow.png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] does research]] Rosetti takes Helstrom to the Blood Hotel, and tells him about what the [[Blood]] does there. Helstrom asks how many patients they have, and Rosetti does not answer. Helstrom notices that the man at the desk is dead and shows Rosetti, who finds a trail of blood going down the stairs. Rosetti says that she should have told him sooner, and that it was now too late.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS105}}
*Rosetti and Helstrom begin packing up the information the Blood kept at the hotel, putting boxes in Helstrom's car.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}

====23rd====
*[[Jolene Spivey]] leads her children into a secure room. As they ask why, Spivey asks them to stay in the room and be quiet. The children agree, and Spivey closes the door on them. Spivey balls her hand in a fist several times, working up courage. She approaches who she believes to be her [[Keith Spivey|husband]], but is in fact a [[Demons|demon]] named [[Basar]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*[[File:BasarBitesSpivey.png|thumb|250px|[[Jolene Spivey]] is bitten by [[Basar]]]] She sees her "husband" scouring their house and asks what he is looking for, asking where he was. Basar responds simply that he had been away, and Spivey reveals that the police believe that he helped [[Hock|two]] [[Liddle|patients]] [[Liberation of Basar|escape]] [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]]. Basar resumes searching as Spivey begs to know what is happening. Basar finds his host's hospital ID badge and approaches Spivey. He grabs her and bites her lip, despite her screams. He puts Spivey in the trunk of the car he and [[Raum]] are using.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Basar exits the house and gets in the car as Raum drives away. Spivey's children watch the car leave from inside the house.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*At Saint Teresa's, [[Ana Helstrom]] and [[Chris Yen]] eat potato chips. Yen asks if Helstrom brought napkins, and Helstrom comments that he is back to being high-maintenance. She tells Yen that she has covered for him with his [[Derrick Jackson|boyfriend]] for twenty-four hours since she did not want him to send the police to their office. She asks Yen what the [[Keeper]] said to him, but Yen said that he could simply feel what it wanted.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*[[File:YenAndAnaInCell.png|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] and [[Ana Helstrom]] talk]] Yen apologizes for trying to kill [[Victoria Helstrom]], although Ana Helstrom insists that he would have been doing them a favor, even if [[Daimon Helstrom]] would have been angry. Yen says that Ana Helstrom did not always hate her mother, confusing Helstrom. Yen reminds Helstrom that when she first got to their foster home, she would consistently cry for her mother and that they would hide in the basement together until it stopped. Yen tells Helstrom that it is okay to miss her mother, and Helstrom asks if he is done. Yen continues to lecture her, so Helstrom gets up to leave. Helstrom asks him not to lecture her, but Yen goes on to say that Helstrom should consider herself lucky her mother is alive. Helstrom says that she will talk to her and notices that Yen is still picking at his arm. Helstrom goes to leave and Yen tries to follow, but Helstrom makes him stay in the room.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*As the door closes behind Helstrom, Yen rushes up to it and shouts to Helstrom that the [[Keeper's Skull]] needs him. Helstrom asks the security guard, [[Ellis]], to tell her and [[Louise Hastings]] if Yen continues to shout. Ellis says that patients usually calm down after they have had their medicine, but Helstrom insists that Yen is a different case.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Daimon Helstrom covers a body at the [[Blood Hotel]] and tells [[Gabriella Rosetti]] that he put boxes in his car. Rosetti asks what Hastings told Helstrom, and Helstrom reports that [[Caretaker]] is not answering his phone, sharing that he does not know why he brought her to the hotel or why Hastings never told him about it. Rosetti says that Helstrom would have tried to shut it down, which the [[Blood]] would not have liked, although Helstrom replies that he does not care.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Rosetti says that Helstrom should return to his mother, and Helstrom assures Rosetti that she did the right thing bringing him to the hotel. Rosetti says that she should have done so sooner, but Helstrom says that the [[Liberation of the Blood Hotel Patients|massacre]] was not her fault. Rosetti suggests the victims get a proper burial, and Helstrom says that they will get one. Rosetti asks if Helstrom thinks his [[Marduk Kurios|father]] is responsible, and Helstrom replies that they would have seen more chaos if it was not done by a powerful demon.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Rosetti asks what Helstrom's father wants with the liberated patients, and Helstrom says that he does not know. Rosetti is hesitant to leave and see the bodies, and Helstrom assures her that he covered them. They leave the office together and see [[Yessenia Flores]] alive. They approach Flores wearily and realize she is dying.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*[[File:YesseniaExorcised.png|thumb|250px|[[Yessenia Flores]] is exorcised]] Helstrom goes to comfort her, and Rosetti gives last rights. Flores falls into Rosetti's arms as Helstrom asks her name. Flores tells them her name and dies as Rosetti finishes the rites.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Ana Helstrom buys a sandwich from the cafeteria, and [[Louise Hastings]] asks why she hasn't seen each other, surprising Helstrom, who believed that her brother was with her. Hastings tells Helstrom about the [[Blood Hotel]] and the escape, and Helstrom guesses that her father is responsible. Helstrom tries to call Caretaker, but Hastings says that he has not been answering. Hastings asks Helstrom to stay with her mother, upsetting Helstrom. Hastings insists that Helstrom needs to make a connection with her mother. Helstrom responds sarcastically, but Hastings urges her not to take their time for granted, and Helstrom reluctantly agrees. Hastings asks Helstrom not to tell her mother about the missing patients or victims.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Helstrom comments on the backpack that Victoria Helstrom is using to hold the [[Keeper's Skull]] at bay, and Victoria explains that she needs to keep the skull close. Ana comments that the bag should have stayed lost, and Victoria asks if she is talking about her. Victoria thanks Ana for getting her a sandwich, and Ana says that she was already getting stuff for [[Chris Yen]]. Victoria asks about Yen, and she shortly says that he is fine.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*[[File:AnaTalksToVictoriaAboutPast.png|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] reminisces with her [[Victoria Helstrom|mother]]]] Victoria asks where Ana is living, and she says that she is in [[San Francisco]]. Victoria attempts to bond by talking about her experience in San Francisco, but Ana cuts her off and asks to stop the small talk, which she despises. Ana asks if Victoria knew that her husband was a serial killer, and Victoria says that she did not. Ana refuses to believe her and presses her, and Victoria explains that Ana's father's charm overwhelmed and blinded her. Victoria asks if Ana has ever been in love, and explains that every time she thought she saw darkness, he turned back into the person she married until he started giving her gifts from his victims, which led her to figure out that he was not who he said. Ana asks why Victoria did not take her children and run. Victoria tells her that her husband only let her see him because he wanted her to. Ana comments that Victoria's hospital room is depressing and suggests changing things up.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Rosetti speeds down the highway, wanting to get to the hospital before Daimon Helstrom's father. Helstrom suggests trying to find Flores' family, but Rosetti asks what they should tell them. She says that Helstrom must have a lot to ask his mother, but Helstrom says that he does not know where to start, wanting just to be happy to see his mother. Rosetti says that she read his files and that they have been through a lot. Helstrom blames himself for getting his mother committed, and Rosetti reassures him, suggesting he empathize with himself. They get a flat tire and begin going to a gas station.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Rosetti and Helstrom get to [[Crescent Heights Service]] and assess the damage, realizing that they will need to call a tow truck. They are approached by a man who offers to fix it, and Helstrom hesitantly agrees. Helstrom calls Hastings, who tells him that [[Caretaker]] still has not answered. Helstrom promises to get to the hospital quickly, and Hastings says that his sister is with his mother, and that they have not hurt each other yet. She insists that they need the time together and hangs up on him. Frustrated, Helstrom goes inside to get coffee, and Rosetti follows.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*'''[[Escape from Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]]''':
**[[Ellis]] watches security footage and is approached by [[Basar]], who repeatedly bangs his head against the table while Ellis struggles and fails to activate the alarm.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Basar enters the secure ward and busts open the door to [[Victoria Helstrom]]'s room, expecting to find [[Kthara]], but is scared to find the room empty.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Outside, Victoria Helstrom comments on how beautiful it is, and asks Ana Helstrom if she remembers the botanical gardens where they used to live, reminiscing on their time there. Ana talks about how Victoria hated the gifts her father would give her, and Victoria explains that she could not tell her daughter. Ana asks why he gave the gifts to her, and Victoria explains that her husband thought that she was like her father, but that Victoria sees as much of herself as him. They reminisce about going to the zoo together. Ana suggests going back inside, and Victoria says that Daimon Helstrom should have moved on.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**At the gas station, Daimon Helstrom and Rosetti try to pay, but find that the cashier is gone, becoming suspicious. They check on their car and find it lifted, hearing a clattering from the garage. Helstrom tells Rosetti to lock the door and enters the garage. Although Rosetti asks where he is going, she then goes in the car.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Helstrom enters the garage and finds the mechanic dead. He is greeted by [[Naren]], who says that he was never good at restraint. Naren says that the demon who sent him was hoping to keep Helstrom busy.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:RosettiScreaming.png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] screams for help]] Rosetti gets out of the car and walks toward the garage, only to get attacked by "[[Brian]]." Rosetti calls out for Helstrom.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Naren says that he is not impressed by Helstrom, who throws him against a car.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**"Brian" drags Rosetti away from the gas station while she calls out for Helstrom.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Naren rights himself as Helstrom drops a shelf full of tires on the demon.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Rosetti bites "Brian's" arm, causing him to let go and drop her. Brian pulls out a knife and threatens to cut her open. However, he finds himself suddenly on fire as he is burnt alive by Helstrom using his demonic ability. Helstrom collapses as Rosetti rushes over to help her. Helstrom says that he could not stop himself from hurting "Brian," but Rosetti says that he would have killed her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Ana Helstrom brings Victoria Helstrom back into [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]] and reflects on her kidnapping. She tells Victoria the truth about her father, and Victoria asks how to kill him. Ana says that she does not know, and asks her not to lose the [[Keeper's Skull]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:EllisCorpse.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Ellis]] is found dead]] [[Louise Hastings]] goes into [[Edgar Lawrence]]'s office to ask about [[Luis (Patient)|Luis]] and finds [[Ellis]]'s corpse, shocking her. She quickly leaves the office.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Hastings opens a safe in her office and retrieves a baton. She orders a guard to lock down the ward.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**The guard walks past Ana and Victoria, prompting Ana to ask if her father was there. Hastings tells her that someone is. Ana unties her mother's handcuffs and asks where her brother is. The security guard returns and says that somebody has locked them in the building. The power goes out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Lawrence pleads with [[Basar]], [[Raum]], and another demon not to kill him. Basar marks Lawrence for possession, and he becomes possessed by [[Magoth]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Several patients begin banging against their doors, begging to be let out of their rooms.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**While driving back to the hospital, Daimon Helstrom warns Ana Helstrom that they had been set up by their father over the phone, telling her that he and Rosetti were attacked and that demons were going to the hospital. Ana realizes that they are already there.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:Hel 106-0623r.jpg|thumb|250px|The group sees [[Magoth]]]] Ana, Victoria Helstrom, and Hastings enter Hastings' office and find Magoth, who greets them. Magoth steals the skull and runs away. Ana tells Hastings to stay with Victoria, but Hastings says that they should wait for Daimon. Ana says that the skull is the only way to stop her father, but Hastings reminds Ana that "her father" nearly killed her the last time they fought. They hear an alarm going off.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**All of the doors in the secure ward open, releasing the patients. The patients wander out and begin walking around. Yen exits his room and looks around, picking at his arm. He sees an axe hanging in case of emergency and takes it, continuing to walk.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Daimon Helstrom and Rosetti pull up to the hospital, and Rosetti refuses to stay in the car. Helstrom breaks the door open and they go inside.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Ana Helstrom and Hastings enter the common area, where they see several patients. Hastings asks [[Tanya]] to return to her room and put on socks, and she agrees. Hastings sees [[Jeff]] and [[Manny (Patient)|Manny]] fighting. Hastings asks Helstrom to stop them, and she grabs Jeff while Hastings sedates him and tells Manny to return to his room. Hastings explains that these are nonviolent patients, and Helstrom continues looking. Helstrom attempts to convince Hastings to stay with her mother, but Hastings refuses.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Hastings apologizes for not taking Helstrom in as a child, saying that she did not believe herself strong enough to care for Helstrom. Helstrom tells Hastings to try not to get killed and resumes searching.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Helstrom searches for her father and goes into the basement of the hospital, when she gets attacked by a demon. She pushes the demon back, and [[Raum]] tells her that "her father" said that they were allowed to kill her, but Helstrom says that he came for her. The other demon again attacks her, but is stopped by Hastings, who fights the demon while Helstrom engages with Raum.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:Ana Chokes two Demons.png|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] defeats [[Raum]]]] Hastings' demon pushes her down while Helstrom pushes Raum down. The other demon rushes to Helstrom, who grabs her by the neck. Helstrom grabs Raum by the neck and lifts them both up, exerting her demonic power on them. Hastings watches, scared, as Helstrom drops both demons, unconscious.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Hastings asks what Helstrom did, and Helstrom says that they are not dead, simply unconscious.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Victoria Helstrom sits in Hastings' office and sees a demon stare into a security camera from the monitor. She watches the door as the demon breaks in and attacks her, but is suddenly thrown backward by Daimon Helstrom, who rushes in and hugs her mom, followed by Rosetti. Daimon introduces Rosetti and asks where the skull is.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Magoth watches the skull and says to it that once his boss arrives, they will destroy it. He is suddenly attacked by [[Chris Yen]], wielding an axe.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:YenWithSkull (Leviathan).png|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] regains the [[Keeper's Skull]]]] Lawrence's body lays on the ground while Yen holds the skull. Ana Helstrom and Hastings find him, and Helstrom expresses annoyance with Yen's obsession. Helstrom asks Yen how he is feeling, and Yen says that Yen got the skull for Helstrom, since it could stop her father. Helstrom reaches out for it, but Yen defensively holds it back. Helstrom tells Yen that she remembers hiding in [[Fowler]]'s workshop, admitting that she missed her mother. Yen hands the skull to Helstrom, who thanks him and places it in its backpack.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Helstrom, Hastings, Yen keep running and find Daimon Helstrom, Victoria Helstrom, and Rosetti. Daimon says they need to get Victoria out, and Ana says they need to stop their father. Although Daimon says they cannot do that without the skull, Ana simply says that she knows. Ana suggests figuring out another way to get [[Kthara]] out of her. When Daimon says that there is not one, Ana says that they will at least know where their mother is, whereas if they do not stop their father now he will go on a killing spree.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Victoria asks for a say in her own future, saying that she failed at keeping her children safe. Daimon attempts to comfort her, and Victoria expresses her wish that her husband had [[Kidnapping of Ana Helstrom|abducted]] him instead of Ana. She expresses pride in Daimon for calling the police on him, saying that Ana is right and they need to end their father's killing as a family.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:BasarArrivesWithSparks.png|thumb|250px|[[Basar]] attacks the group]] The elevator arrives on their floor and they prepare to use it, when "their father" bursts into the room and throws Yen, Ana, Hastings, and Rosetti back,{{Ref|HS106}} marking Rosetti for possession.{{Ref|HS108}} He grabs Victoria by the throat and pushes her into the elevator. He seals the elevator shut as Daimon tries to pull it open. Ana rights herself and suggests they take the stairs. Daimon rushes to check on Rosetti, who says that she is fine, and Ana yells at Daimon to move. The siblings leave as the others right themselves.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Ana and Daimon make it to the service area as "their father" threatens to kill them. Ana realizes that the [[Keeper]] is destroying his [[Keith Spivey|host]]. Ana approaches and taunts "her father," driving him away from Victoria while Daimon rushes over to her. Ana and "her father" fight, and "her father" kicks her into a nearby car, causing the skull to fall onto the floor.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Daimon gets angry, threatening "his father." He throws a wood pillar at "his father" which he avoids, followed by an air conditioner, which he also avoids. The two attempt to fight in hand-to-hand combat, but the "Helstrom father" throws Daimon to the side.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Ana sees "her father" attack and fight Daimon, who holds back one of his punches and pushes Daimon to the ground. Victoria hides underneath a truck and Ana watches as "her father" grabs at and hits Daimon.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Victoria reaches for the skull, which had rolled under the truck.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:Basar'sDemonMouth.png|thumb|250px|[[Basar]] opens his mouth tp kill [[Daimon Helstrom|Helstrom]]]] Ana falls off the car she was thrown onto and rights herself.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**The "Helstrom father" hits Helstrom again.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Victoria continues to reach for the skull.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Daimon taunts "his father," saying that he could never break the familial bond between him, his family, and his sister. "His father" opens the stomach in his chest, preparing to consume Daimon.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Victoria grabs the skull under the truck and backs out.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**The "Helstrom father" stands over Daimon, while Victoria shows Ana the skull. Ana gets the skull and shoves it into "her father's" stomach, causing him to fall over in pain. Ana helps Daimon up as "their father's" host body burns in front of them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**[[File:BasarTakenByKthara.png|thumb|250px|[[Basar]] is saved by [[Kthara]]]] Ana and Daimon see that the demon is still alive after the fire dies down, and Ana says that she is nothing like her father and never will be. "Her father" grabs her ankle, causing her to realize that he is not her father, rather the demon [[Basar]]. Basar laughs as [[Kthara]] regains control of Victoria's body and pulls him onto the truck.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
**Daimon calls after his mother, who says that she hopes he said goodbye to Victoria before closing the truck. [[Raum]] drives the truck out of the hospital. Daimon says that they will find her and that their father will never recover, but Ana tells him that they were not fighting their father.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS106}}
*Daimon Helstrom exorcises the demons left behind at the hospital.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Rosetti struggles to sleep, only getting a few hours.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}

====24th====
*[[Raum]] finds someone on the street with enough drugs to keep Kthara's host body alive. The person does no cooperate, so Raum brutally beats them and gets the drugs.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:Helstrom demon patient.png|thumb|250px|[[Loman]] enters]] Cleanup occurs at [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]] following the [[Escape from Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health|attack]] the previous night. [[Loman]] his brought into a room. He stares into a security camera and is escorted inside.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[Daimon Helstrom]] watches Loman on the security camera as [[Ana Helstrom]] talks about mistaking [[Basar]] for her [[Marduk Kurios|father]]. Daimon comments on their state, scolding her for believing it. Ana defends herself and says that their father is out there, saying that he will be back. Daimon asks for proof when he comes, and says that he is judging himself for going against his gut, and says that she seems not to care that their [[Victoria Helstrom|mother]] is missing, taunting her for being easily manipulated by Basar. Daimon attempts to walk away, but Ana follows and continues the argument.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Outside the hospital, [[Louise Hastings]] asks [[Gabriella Rosetti]] if she got sleep. Rosetti says she only got a few hours and tells Hastings to worry about Daimon Helstrom, who is tired. Hastings says that she is glad that Rosetti has come to like Helstrom, resolving to go inside and check on him and his sister.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:RosettiSeesJolene.png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] is startled to see [[Jolene Spivey]]]] Rosetti prepares to follow Hastings inside, but hears a thud coming from a nearby car. She opens the trunk of the car and finds [[Jolene Spivey]] inside, begging for help from her "[[Basar|husband]]." Rosetti helps Spivey out of the trunk and brings her inside.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Ana Helstrom scolds Daimon Helstrom for keeping [[Kthara]] locked up and letting her grow, having gotten tricked into believing that he could save her. Ana insists that she would not have let her hope get that far, and Daimon says that she got what she wanted, sacrificing their mother to kill the demon. She says that their mom told her to do it, but Daimon asks why Ana insists on using her first name, but Ana says that she is no longer their mother.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Hastings walks in as Daimon calls Ana coldhearted, and Hastings tells them to stop, saying that they were all tricked. Ana yells at her, telling her to stay out of the family business, but Daimon yells at Ana, saying that Hastings is family and does not need Ana's disrespect. Ana says that she does not need the situation and decides to leave. As Ana leaves the office, Daimon yells that he will find their mother without her so she can pretend they do not exist and to go back to business as usual.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[Chris Yen]] picks at his arm as Ana Helstrom enters his room and tells him that they are leaving. Yen is relieved and quickly gets up.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Rosetti leads Spivey through the hospital and passes Helstrom and Yen. Helstrom angrily says goodbye to Rosetti, who calls after her regarding her mother. Helstrom keeps walking and says that she is not her problem while Yen rushes after Helstrom.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:Portland Harbor.png|thumb|250px|[[Raum]] returns with medicine]]Raum brings medicine to [[Portland Harbor]] and boards the ''[[Garibaldi II]]'', where [[Kthara]] is keeping an injured [[Basar]]. Kthara says that her body is failing, and Raum reports that he found drugs.  Kthara says that he should have brought the seller, and Raum says that Basar is too damaged, suggesting they move on. Kthara throws Raum back and says that they will not leave her son. Basar coughs up blood and Kthara comments on his state. Raum says that he cannot mark another person, and Kthara asks why he would need to.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:JoleneSpivey107.png|thumb|250px|[[Jolene Spivey]] talks about her experience]] Daimon Helstrom heals Spivey's mark.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Hastings tends to Spivey's wounds and asks what Helstrom did, and Hastings explains that he healed her. Hastings reassures her that she will be okay, and Spivey insists that it was not her husband who attacked her. Hastings says that she believes her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Rosetti asks as to why Basar would mark Spivey but leave her behind, suggesting they forgot about her. Helstrom explains that they were saving her for someone, and Rosetti suggests that it was Kthara. Hastings leaves her office expresses sympathy for Spivey, saying that Helstrom saving her is the only good thing that has happened recently. Helstrom says that Kthara will need a new host. Rosetti asks how many more facilities like the [[Blood Hotel]] there are, and Hastings says that while [[Caretaker]] would know, he still will not answer. Helstrom states his intent to interrogate [[Loman]], but Hastings and Rosetti encourage him to rest. Daimon tells Hastings not to bother with Caretaker, who he says can take care of himself.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}

====25th====
*[[File:CaretakerWalksOutOfVan.png|thumb|250px|[[Caretaker]] is taken to his destination]] [[Caretaker]] is tied up in his van with a bag over his head. The bag is removed as [[Lee (Blood)|Lee]] tells him that his allegiances are under question. He tells Caretaker about the [[Liberation of the Blood Hotel Patients|massacre]] at the [[Blood Hotel]], surprising Caretaker. The car arrives at Caretaker's [[Caretaker's House|house]] and Caretaker is taken out of the van. [[Esther Smith]] comes outside and welcomes him home.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[Daimon Helstrom]] dreams about [[Kthara]] asking him to let his demonic side out, and [[Gabriella Rosetti]] wakes him up. Helstrom gets up and denies Rosetti's suggestion to rest at his [[Daimon Helstrom's House|house]], instead resolving to interrogate [[Loman]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Rosetti asks Loman where Kthara is, and Loman simply says that she is where she needs to be. Helstrom reveals that they healed Kthara's vessel, and Loman explains that being stuck in his host at the Blood Hotel was worse than whatever the demons will do to them. He talks about his experience of being trapped in his host's mind. He calls Helstrom a traitor, but Helstrom insists that he is not one of them. Loman says that he will end up vilified  and separated from those he loves.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Loman suggests he join the demons, saying that the humans started the war and the demons only wanted freedom. Helstrom threatens to exorcise him as Loman explains that only Kthara can grant that freedom. Loman snaps his host's neck, shocking Rosetti.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:DerrickYenTalk.png|thumb|250px|[[Chris Yen]] talks to [[Derrick Jackson]]]] [[Chris Yen]] sees his boyfriend, [[Derrick Jackson]], and lies to him about his whereabouts the past few days.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[Louise Hastings]] meets with Archbishop [[Terrazi]] and asks for help tracking down Caretaker. Terrazi asks why him, and Hastings explains that Caretaker works with the [[Blood]]. Hastings asks Terrazi to contact the Blood, believing that he can do so directly. Hastings talks about their facilities, and Terrazzo denies knowledge. Hastings says that lives are on the line and that she needs him to contact the Blood.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Terrazi reminds Hastings that he warned her about Daimon Helstrom long ago, but Hastings scolds him, again asking him to call. Hastings asks Terrazi to tell them that there is a monster looking for a new host. Terrazi says that he can make that call. Hastings prepares to leave, and Terrazi tells her that Rosetti may want to consider other jobs since the church cannot guarantee her safety on her current path.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[Ana Helstrom]] sits in her [[Ana Helstrom's Auction House|auction house]] and is approached by Yen, who asks about her. Helstrom suggests going to work, but Yen says that he is only there because he forgot his phone charger. Yen tells Helstrom to go home, but Helstrom insists that she is alright. Yen scolds Helstrom for having him lie to his boyfriend, who knows something is off. Helstrom yells at Yen, but he cuts her off and suggests that he should have stayed to fight her brother, or that she should calm down. Helstrom asks Yen to help her kill someone.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Smith tells Caretaker that she heard about Hastings asking after her and that Kthara escaped. Caretaker asks to do his job, but Smith says that he failed to keep the Helstrom siblings at bay. He defends them, and Smith asks why he continues picking the wrong side. Caretaker explains that the Helstroms are on their side. Smith expresses surprise that he kept the house, taunting him about the death of his family.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Smith approaches Caretaker's collection of knives and asks which he found with Ana Helstrom, but Caretaker says that he buried the knife she is referring to. Smith does not believe her and orders Lee to open Caretaker's shirt, which he does. Smith takes a knife and tests it against Caretaker's scar, explaining that they can no longer put demons in comas and that they need a weapon that kills demons.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Ana Helstrom and Yen guide a buyer through their auction house. Helstrom asks for a moment and Yen says that they are not killing for a while, having decided since he is the only rational one at the moment. Helstrom threatens to search for a target, asking him to do it the right way. Yen explains that they should not kill to fill a void, and Helstrom asks if he will help. Yen talks about covering for Helstrom's first kill, saying that he wants no part of killing to scratch an itch. Helstrom knocks a crate over between them, not affecting Yen. Yen says that Jackson will be visiting later and returns to their client.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:DaimonWalkingInStreet.png|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] walks in the street]] Daimon Helstrom walks through Portland and stops outside an antique store. He goes to text his sister an apology, but chooses not to. Helstrom gets a call from Caretaker's phone and talks to Smith, who offers an alliance. Although Helstrom is hesitant, Smith says that Kthara's hunt could reunite them. Smith says that they need his help killing Kthara, but Helstrom refuses. Smith explains that they respected Caretaker and Hastings' decision to separate him from his sister, and Helstrom hangs up the phone.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Yen and Jackson eat lunch, and Yen asks what is wrong. Jackson says that he felt as though Yen ghosted him and asks him to manage his work-life balance. He jokes that Ana Helstrom has blackmail on him, suggesting a video of him [[Assassination of Cameron Tate|murdering]] [[Cameron Tate|someone]]. Yen simply explains that it is hard to leave because he has known Helstrom for a long time. Helstrom arrives and asks if they will take a long time. Jackson tells Helstrom her behavior is unacceptable, suggesting she find a way to relieve her stress. Helstrom thanks Jackson for sharing and glares at Yen before walking away.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:CaretakerTortured.png|thumb|250px|[[Caretaker]] is stabbed]] Lee picks up a knife, which Caretaker assures Lee is not the one he wants. Lee tests it against Caretaker's scar anyway, so Caretaker explains that it is a man-made fake. Smith enters as Caretaker talks about the innocent lives lost during the looting of Baghdad, asking if he believes Helstrom to be innocent. Caretaker insists that she should be judged by her own mistakes, not those of her [[Marduk Kurios|father]]. However, Smith calls her a mistake, prompting Caretaker to get defensive.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Smith comments that she will never understand why he is soft on Helstrom and picks up another knife. She touches it to Caretaker's scar and it sizzles, commenting that it is not buried. Caretaker pleads with Smith not to hunt the Helstroms, asking if they want to bring out the best or worst in the siblings and refusing to help bring out the worst. Smith orders Lee to untie Caretaker.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Hastings attempts to explain that she wanted to tell Daimon Helstrom about her choice to separate him from his sister, but could not find the right time. She explains that they were separated to keep them alive. She accepts responsibility, claiming that his sister's presence would be problematic because of her experience. She says that his sister showed a predilection for violence, and that she did not want to jeopardize Helstrom's own healing. Helstrom suggests that Hastings is blaming him, so Hastings apologizes again. Helstrom asks if she thought about his feelings about being separated from his sister, and Hastings admits that his sister scares her.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:DerrickConfrontsYen.png|thumb|250px|[[Derrick Jackson]] argues with [[Chris Yen]]]] Ana Helstrom works on her laptop while Yen polishes an artifact. He sees Helstrom looking through the [[San Francisco Police Department]]'s database, scolding her for planning another murder carelessly. Helstrom deflects when the buzzer sounds. Helstrom answers as Jackson storms in, demanding to know how he is logged into the database in the auction house. Yen denies knowledge of it, and Jackson says that he has to know why each file was accessed. He tells Yen that he will find out what is happening and leave. Helstrom glares at Jackson.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*At home, Daimon Helstrom looks at his drink and hears a knock on the door. He opens it to find [[Gabriella Rosetti]] and tries to turn her away. She enters the house and sits with him, asking if Hastings heard from Caretaker. Helstrom says that Caretaker was okay, and Helstrom gets upset with himself for allowing [[Loman]] to kill his host. Rosetti attempts to comfort him, telling him about a time her parents requested an exorcism to treat what was revealed to be epilepsy. She says that she has not had a seizure in years and explains that she forgave her parents when she realized they were faced with a difficult choice. She tells Helstrom to forgive himself.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Helstrom expresses regret for the way he spoke to his sister, but Rosetti insists that she was the one who walked away. Helstrom says that she was right to, and suggests that Rosetti do the same. Rosetti says that she is not leaving, and lets go of Helstrom's hand as the moment becomes intimate. Rosetti suggests making a plan for Helstrom's [[Victoria Helstrom|mother]], but Helstrom says that they need help from the [[Blood]].{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Helstrom calls Smith, who smiles and answers.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:Derrick"Hugged"ByAna.png|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] uses her powers on [[Derrick Jackson]]]] Ana Helstrom waits outside the [[San Francisco Police Station]] and watches as Jackson leaves for the day. She follows him to his car, but he notices her and turns around. He asks what she is doing there, and she confesses to having accessed the database without his knowledge. She explains that she wanted to screen her clients after [[Edward Tate]] ended up being a criminal. She says that Yen means a lot to her, asking to reconcile and promising she will not access the database again. The two hug and Helstrom starts to drain his life force, but remembers her escape from her father and decides against it. She asks if Jackson is okay and leaves in a hurry, overwhelmed as she remembers running from her father.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*[[File:BasarDrawsSymbol.png|thumb|250px|[[Basar]] communicates with [[Kthara]]]] On the ''[[Garibaldi II]]'', [[Raum]] injects [[Basar]] with medicine while [[Kthara]] comforts him. Kthara tells Basar to save his energy as she tries to speak. He takes some of his [[Keith Spivey|host body]]'s blood to draw a spiral on the wall, communicating to Kthara that he had marked a new host.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Yen works in the auction house and notices his bite marks bleeding through his bandages. Ana Helstrom returns and confronts her box of gifts from her father as she reflects on her father burying her alive. She picks up the box and looks inside, remembering getting rescued by Caretaker. Helstrom throws the box to the ground and starts crying as she notices a necklace. Yen approaches Helstrom, who apologizes for almost doing something. Yen assures her that she did not do it and that she is not her father. Helstrom says that her family needs her, and Yen tells her that they do, including himself.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Helstrom and Rosetti arrive at the place he agreed to meet with the Blood, and Helstrom says that while he is not sure about working with the Blood, they have an extensive network and Caretaker can broker peace. Helstrom asks Rosetti to stay in the car, but Rosetti opens the door.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*Helstrom and Rosetti enter the building and find Caretaker missing. Helstrom assures Rosetti that they will not attack, but has doubts as Lee and two other men approach them. Lee explains that Caretaker is in their van and Smith will explain what is happening after they check him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
*'''[[Ambush on Daimon Helstrom]]''':
**Helstrom hesitantly turns around for the search, when Lee tries to stab him with his father's [[Shard|dagger]]. Helstrom stops him telekinetically and throws the other two men to the side. Helstrom turns around to see his father's blade, demanding to know where they got it. He gets angry as a man shoots at him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}
**[[File:Daimon's Scar and Screaming.png|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] loses control]] Helstrom falls and gets angry as his scar burns. He sets two of the men on fire as he screams and Rosetti watches in horror. Smith backs away as Helstrom releases Lee. Lee falls to the ground and rushes to catch up to Smith as she drives away, dropping the knife. Helstrom picks it up as Rosetti approaches him, scared. Helstrom locks eyes with Rosetti and breathes deeply.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS107}}

====26th====
*As [[Daimon Helstrom]] and [[Gabriella Rosetti]] arrive at Helstrom's [[Daimon Helstrom's House|house]], Helstrom leaves a voicemail for [[Ana Helstrom]], demanding that she answer her phone, since the [[Blood]] might attack her. Rosetti tells Helstrom to go to the hospital or call the police, but Helstrom explains that he would be turning himself in for attempted murder if he did that.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Helstrom enters his house and starts changing his clothes angrily, when Rosetti gets him to stop. She realizes that his injury is already healing and assures Helstrom that the attack was not his fault. Helstrom continues to blame himself and realizes that Rosetti has his [[Marduk Kurios|father]]'s [[Shard|dagger]]. Rosetti reveals it as Helstrom explains that it gave him his scar. Rosetti realized that it belonged to his father.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Helstrom walks out of his room and looks at the dagger, telling Rosetti that his scar is the only thing he never healed from. Rosetti asks if the Blood could have killed him, and Helstrom realizes that the dagger has an old and violent feeling, realizing that his sister must have felt it more strongly. Rosetti tells Helstrom they need to get rid of it, but Helstrom says they need to get rid of the other one as well, confusing Rosetti.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*[[File:BasarMurderedByKthara.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Basar]] is willingly killed by [[Kthara]]]] On the ''[[Garibaldi II]]'', [[Kthara]] sings to [[Basar]]. [[Raum]] arrives and approaches Kthara, who scolds him for arriving empty-handed. Kthara says that they will have help soon from [[Magoth|someone]] who is loyal. Raum asks about Basar, so Kthara reminds him of the suffering Basar has endured, which she claims is important to remember. She tells Basar to rest and continues singing as she turns Basar on his side and rips his heart out of his [[Keith Spivey|host]]. She tells Raum to find the new hosts and take care of Basar.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Helstrom sits in his car outside [[Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health]] and reflects on fighting his father.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*[[Louise Hastings]] enters her office and gets scared when she sees [[Gabriella Rosetti]] in there. Rosetti explains she left something for Hastings to hide, revealing that the Blood attacked. Hastings blames herself for the attack.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*While Helstrom drives, Rosetti explains that Archbishop [[Terrazi]] warned her about the attack. Rosetti confesses that she gave Terrazi information, believing him to be honest since he was a man of faith. Helstrom jokes that she should know better than to put her faith in men, but Rosetti insists that she has faith in him. Helstrom suggests that she should not and gets a call from Ana Helstrom, revealing that she is safe.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Daimon expresses concern that Ana would not have returned, and Ana admits that she let her anger get the better of her. Daimon apologizes for judging her, but Ana says she was about to apologize. Daimon tells Ana that he was about to say she was right, so Ana suggests they talk in person. Daimon reveals that he is going to their [[Helstrom Residence|childhood home]], prompting her to ask why. Daimon says that they are getting the other piece of their father's knife, suggesting they could use it to kill Kthara. Ana says that it would kill their [[Victoria Helstrom|mother]], but Daimon says that they will not get their mother back. Ana asks why he referred to "the other piece."{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*As Hastings locks her safe, Ana Helstrom enters and demands to see the knife. Hastings hesitantly takes it out of the safe and shows it to her, allowing her to feel its energy. She tells Hastings that it is toxic, and Hastings coughs up blood.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*[[File:Blood.png|thumb|250px|[[Esther Smith]] talks to [[Ahmad]]]] [[Esther Smith]] compliments [[Ahmad]]'s work on a knife while [[Finn Miller]] asks to be let out of the cage. Smith explains that he is likely to be Kthara's new host so that they can put her in a coma until they get a weapon that will kill her. Smith reminds Miller of their oath to kill the Helstrom father, insisting that they owe it to their deceased relatives. Ahmad reports that they found Daimon Helstrom, and Smith tells Miller to remember what they are fighting for.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Ana Helstrom pours a drink and insists they lock the knife away, suggesting it is threatening Hastings. However, Hastings says that it is not magic as she accepts the drink with a shaky hand. Hastings confesses that she has cancer, shocking Helstrom. Hastings explains that [[Caretaker]] is the only person who knows. She comments that he left after saying he would stick with her, and Helstrom explains that it is a pattern. Hastings tells Helstrom that he has been torn between the Blood and wanting what was best for Helstrom. Helstrom suggests that Caretaker would not have willingly revealed where the knife was, but Hastings suggests he would have if they planned to use it on Kthara.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Rosetti and Daimon Helstrom arrive at Helstrom's childhood home, and Rosetti comments that the neighborhood is quiet. Helstrom explains that they would always live in a place away from people. Rosetti suggests she talks to the people who live there, but Helstrom is worried that [[demons]] are already present. The door opens while they debate what to do, and a real estate agent puts up an open house sign.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*[[File:MagothAwakensInMiller.png|thumb|250px|[[Magoth]] takes over [[Finn Miller]]]] Miller grunts in pain as he starts to get possessed. [[Ahmad]] threatens the demon with blood from a [[Keeper Demons|Keeper Demon]], but the demon uses telekinesis to attack another man and break free of his chain. He introduces himself as [[Magoth]] and insists that Ahmad got Kthara's name wrong before killing him.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Helstrom and Rosetti walk through the residence as the agent shows off the fireplace. The agent suggests that the house is perfect for children, and Helstrom goes along with the agent’s belief they are in a relationship, claiming they plan on having a lot of children. Helstrom asks if the agent heard anything weird about the house, and she says that it was on the market many times. The agent turns her attention to another couple, who Helstrom realizes are in the Blood. They ask to look around, but the realtor insists on showing them the kitchen.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Magoth arrives at the ''Garibaldi II'' and greets [[Raum]] and [[Kthara]], who compliments his efforts to manipulate the Helstrom siblings. Magoth asks about her vessel being stolen, but Kthara explains that they have [[Daimon Helstrom|new]] [[Gabriella Rosetti|hosts]]. He tells Raum and Magoth to prepare for the hosts to be possessed, reminding them that the timing is essential. Magoth and Raum leave while Kthara lays down and says that they will have new hosts soon.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*[[File:AnaHastingsInCell.png|thumb|250px|[[Ana Helstrom]] and [[Louise Hastings]] talk]] Ana Helstrom lays down in her mother's hospital room, telling Helstrom about her [[Victoria Helstrom|mother]]'s energy in the room. She expresses sympathy with her mother, and tells her that the priest has requested an exorcist, explaining it is a trap for her brother. Helstrom explains that they will not be expecting her, suggesting they use her father's dagger. Hastings insists that it is too dangerous and they should wait for her brother, but Helstrom insists that he would not be able to kill his mother. She asks Hastings for a favor.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Rosetti notices two more members of the Blood, who Helstrom realizes do not know where the knife is. Helstrom asks the realtor if the abandoned barn near the house is part of the property. The realtor offers to see if the owner is willing to sell, and he thanks her. Helstrom returns to Rosetti, who insists that they need a plan. Helstrom claims to have a plan, so Rosetti asks to be filled in. Helstrom suggests that they wait for the Blood to run out of patience.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Ana Helstrom tells Hastings that touching the dagger makes her feel the pain her father inflicted, asking Hastings to kill Kthara. Hastings refuses, but Helstrom asks what Hastings was planning to do. Hastings continues to refuse, but Helstrom scolds her about her mother's suffering. Hastings says that killing someone would haunt her forever, but comments that she does not have long anyway. Helstrom compliments Hastings' dark comment.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Daimon Helstrom stands in the basement of his childhood home, remembering his sister's [[Kidnapping of Ana Helstrom|kidnapping]]. Rosetti tells him that the Blood are leaving, sympathizing with him about the bad memories associated with the house. However, Helstrom explains that they are in the house that felt most like home, saying that his father gave him a normal childhood before the kidnapping.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Helstrom claims that being around him puts Rosetti in danger, but that he is not since he has his father's abilities. Rosetti insists that Helstrom is not his father, but Helstrom claims that part of him is, explaining that his father left the knife and the scar as a reminder of that fact. Rosetti insists that he is a good person, but Helstrom talks about the people he has killed. Rosetti plans to escape, but Helstrom says that he is not leaving without the dagger. He says that if the Blood try to stop him, he will show them who he is.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Search for the Shard]]''': [[File:Daimon with shovel.png|thumb|200px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] digs for the [[Shard]]]] Helstrom digs a hole in the abandoned barn, getting upset as he remembers his time accidentally using his abilities against a group of bullies. Helstrom picks up a box from the ground and becomes surrounded by the armed Blood, who attack him. Helstrom fights through the Blood, who taze him and put a [[Keeper Talisman]] on his forehead. A woman picks up the box and finds an action figure inside as Helstrom burns through the Talisman and throws the group back telekinetically, threatening to make an example out of them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Skirmish at Portland Harbor]]''':
**Ana Helstrom and Hastings walk through the ''Garibaldi II'', followed by Raum. They enter Kthara's room, who assumes that they are Helstrom's brother. Helstrom tells Kthara that she is there to kill her, prompting Hastings to reveal the dagger. Kthara asks where they got it and starts telekinetically throwing things at them.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
**Helstrom and Hastings rush to Kthara and pin her down. Hastings tries to stab Kthara, but finds herself being stopped telepathically. Kthara forces Hastings to stab Helstrom with it, causing them both to fall over. Helstrom starts to get overwhelmed by the feelings she is getting from the dagger.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Search for the Shard]]''': Rosetti returns to the barn and tells Daimon Helstrom that all of the Blood had seemingly left, but finds Helstrom standing in front of several Blood members ready to be hanged. Helstrom tells Rosetti to wait outside as he approaches the Blood, making her nervous.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Skirmish at Portland Harbor]]''': Kthara gloats that [[Victoria Helstrom]] will feel the same pain as Ana Helstrom for eternity. Hastings removes the knife from her leg as Kthara asks what Ana believed to be the reason for the knife being her father's favorite weapon. Ana curses at Kthara.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Search for the Shard]]''': [[File:HangedBloodMembers.png|thumb|250px|[[Daimon Helstrom]] attempts to hang the [[Blood]]]] Daimon Helstrom insists to Rosetti that the Blood only understand extremes as he reomves one of the people's platforms, holding him up telekinetically. Helstrom starts to move to another platform while Rosetti pleads with him to stop. Helstrom tells Rosetti to go outside, but Rosetti refuses.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Skirmish at Portland Harbor]]''': Ana Helstrom and Hastings right themselves as Kthara encourages them to kill Helstrom's mother. Kthara lays down as the two women approach her. Kthara grants Victoria Helstrom control, and Victoria smiles at her daughter. Hastings insists it is a lie while Victoria cups Ana's cheek. Ana suggests there is another way to stop Kthara, but Hastings insists that the demon would escape. Ana sends the dagger flying out of Hastings' hands and resolves to save Victoria's life. She takes a pillow and smothers Victoria.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Search for the Shard]]''': Daimon Helstrom removes another platform and sees Rosetti look at him with horror, saying that he knew she would eventually. He explains that he is doing it for [[Esther Smith]], asking her to come out. Smith enters the barn and greets Helstrom.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Skirmish at Portland Harbor]]''':
**Hastings reminds Ana Helstrom that Victoria Helstrom's death would allow Kthara to escape, but Ana asks whether Victoria would be free if they can revive her. Hastings insists that Daimon had already tried everything, but Ana points out that he did not try killing Victoria. Hastings tries to explain that Victoria has a low chance of surviving, but Ana says that there is still a chance.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
**[[File:VictoriaSuffocating.png|thumb|250px|[[Victoria Helstrom]] is nearly killed]] Hastings gets the knife, reminding Ana that she told her they had to use the knife or else she would return. Ana suggests that Kthara has no other body to possess, but Hastings points out that she could return to kill again. Ana says that that will be in the future, but they can save Victoria now. Victoria dies as Ana lifts the pillow. She senses that Victoria is gone and backs up while Hastings does CPR.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Search for the Shard]]''':
**Smith scolds Rosetti for standing by Daimon Helstrom's actions while Rosetti insists that Helstrom is not acting like himself. Helstrom asks Smith to beg for the lives of her men, but Smith tells him to kill them if he intends to, claiming it would prove her point that demons are all the same. Smith tells him that she will be Helstrom forever.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
**Helstrom turns to the Blood members and explains that letting them die is her idea of mercy, lowering them. Rosetti picks up a shovel and threatens Helstrom, who simply says that she does not want to break his concentration. He explains that he is like his father, but that he is also human, giving him a power his father never had. He releases the Blood members and tells Smith that he forgives her for her prejudice and treachery, declaring the Blood's war to be over. He asks that they stay away from his family and tells her to consider himself lucky they went after him as opposed to his sister. Helstrom leaves with Rosetti.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*'''[[Skirmish at Portland Harbor]]''': Hastings continues to perform CPR while Ana Helstrom frantically looks for something to save her mother. Ana yells at Victoria for letting her be the one to kill her, when she breathes and comes to. She tells Ana to use her inside voice, making Ana and Hastings laugh.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Daimon Helstrom breaks into his childhood home and retrieves the second half of the dagger from the fireplace. He looks at it and reflects on Hastings assuring him that he is not a monster.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Helstrom and Rosetti drive home in silence as they reflect on what happened. The two look at each other.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*[[File:Gabriella Rosetti (Underneath).png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] arrives]] Helstrom sits in his [[Daimon Helstrom's House|home]], and Rosetti gives him a drink. Helstrom assures Rosetti that he would have released the Blood members regardless of whether she was there, and Rosetti says that she knew, asking to be filled in on his next plan. Helstrom says that he would like to forget the day, except for how ready she was to tell people they were living in sin. They laugh at Rosetti's lack of familiarity with terms regarding sex.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Helstrom asks what the Vatican would say about a nun having a drink with a demon, but Rosetti says that she is not a nun yet. The two look at each other, when Helstrom's cell phone vibrates. He answers the call, and Ana Helstrom tells him that Victoria Helstrom is free. Daimon tells her that he will be there, but Ana offers to watch her. Daimon thanks Ana, who tells him that she expects him to do the talking in the morning.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Hastings asks the doctor to talk to her about her treatment options.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Daimon Helstrom hangs up the phone and tells Rosetti about his mother. Rosetti smiles and asks if he is okay, and he says that he always thought that he would be the one to free her. He claims that he gave up on her, but Rosetti assures him that he did not. She says that by bringing his sister back, he did save her. They joke about telling his sister that, and Rosetti points out that Helstrom is free as well.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*Rosetti hugs Helstrom, and the two kiss. Helstrom mentions her vows, but Rosetti says that she has not taken any and they resume kissing. Helstrom comments on how he smells, so he leaves to shower and give her a moment. Rosetti paces and looks at her reflection. She takes out her hair clip and pushes it back when she hears a noise.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
*[[File:RosettiLooksAtMarking.png|thumb|250px|[[Gabriella Rosetti]] finds out she is marked]] Rosetti goes to the door while Raum approaches it. Rosetti calls for Helstrom, but hears something get dropped through the mail slot. Rosetti walks toward the door and suddenly feels a sharp pain in her head. She looks in a mirror and sees a mark [[Escape from Saint Teresa Center for Mental Health|left]] by Basar. She starts praying, but falls over as Kthara possesses her. Kthara stands up and finds the item Raum left.{{Ref|HelstromMainPlacement}}{{Ref|HS108}}
